(838, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MSc Energy and Sustainable Development', 'msc-energy-and-sustainable-development', '£', '17600', '500', NULL, '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Society, industry, and policymakers agree that change is needed at all levels to tackle climate change and ensure sustainable development for future generations. At DMU, our Energy and Sustainable Development MSc is designed to provide you with the knowledge and skills needed to make this happen.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You will learn how to achieve sustainable development and reduce carbon emissions through sustainable energy, efficient production, and organizational change. You&rsquo;ll be taught by leading experts from the School of Engineering and Sustainable Development, as well as guest speakers who are specialists in the field.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Learn from scientists and researchers who are actively advancing knowledge and sharing their expertise.<br />\r\n- This course is accredited by the Chartered Institution of Building Services Engineers (CIBSE) and the Energy Institute (EI) until August 2024, with reaccreditation being pursued from September 2024.<br />\r\n- Graduate with the knowledge and skills needed for careers in industry, the public sector, research, or education.<br />\r\n- Access cutting-edge facilities like the Energy Laboratory, a high-tech centre for teaching, research, and technology demonstration.<br />\r\n- Graduates have gone on to work for major organizations like the Carbon Trust, BMW, National Grid, the European Commission, energy and environmental consultancies, and central and local government.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have the equivalent of an Honours degree (2:2 minimum) in a relevant subject or five years of work experience in an appropriate field.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with 5.5 in each band (or equivalent) when you start the course is essential.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-msc-energy-and-sustainable-development', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 15, 15, '2024-08-17 10:59:24', '2024-08-17 11:00:24'),
