(1134, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MA International Film Production', 'ma-international-film-production', '£', '17600', '500', 'Want to pursue a master\'s degree in MA International Film Production in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In our International Film Production MA/PG Dip/PG Cert course, you will improve your filmmaking skills, such as storytelling, lighting, production design, and directing. You&#39;ll also develop essential business and production management skills like post-production, pitching, budgeting, and management.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYour learning will be enriched with insights from industry experts. You&#39;ll explore and analyze global cinema, gaining a deeper understanding of the industry and learning about different directors and film movements worldwide.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Benefit from the expertise of DMU&rsquo;s research groups, including the Cinema and Television History Research Institute (CATHI) and the Institute of Creative Technologies. These groups offer inspiring guest lectures based on their world-class research.<br />\r\n- Use our Creative Technology Studios, equipped with top-quality video, audio, and radio production facilities. You&#39;ll also have access to specialized film production equipment, including exclusive use of Blackmagic Ursa film cameras and Sound Devices 633 Production Audio Mixers.<br />\r\n- Enhance your learning and connect with industry professionals through guest lectures and workshops. Previous speakers include Terry Bamber (Assistant Director of World War Z, Casino Royale, Fast X), Producer Al Clark (London To Brighton, Calibre), and Producer Iain Smith (Mad Max: Fury Road, Planet Of The Apes, Children of Men).</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have a degree similar to a British Honours degree with at least a 2:2 grade in a relevant subject. We are also open to considering equivalent qualifications from any country.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with 5.5 in each band (or equivalent) when you start the course is required.</p>', '<p>Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-ma-international-film-production', 'MA International Film Production | De Montfort University', 'MA International Film Production | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 10:03:47', '2024-08-28 10:03:47'),
(1135, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MA International Relations', 'ma-international-relations', '£', '15800', '500', 'Want to pursue a master\'s degree in MA International Relations in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Our International Relations course explores how global and international politics are often affected by inequalities, such as those related to race, gender, and social class.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nIn this course, you&#39;ll gain a deep understanding of important concepts and theories in international relations and learn to apply them to current global issues like the political economy, development, global governance, security, foreign policy, and inequality in creative and innovative ways.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- You can complete the course with a Postgraduate Diploma or a Postgraduate Certificate, depending on the credits you earn.<br />\r\n- The course covers important global challenges like poverty, inequality, gender issues, democracy, and job security, moving beyond traditional international relations topics.<br />\r\n- By studying real-life experiences, you&#39;ll see how global issues connect with local ones and develop a sense of global responsibility and political awareness.<br />\r\n- You&#39;ll learn and practice skills that will help you work towards a fair, peaceful, and sustainable world.<br />\r\n- Benefit from expert teaching and additional opportunities like study trips, guest speakers, and events organized by our research centres.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have a degree equivalent to a 2:2 UK bachelor&rsquo;s degree in politics, international relations, or a related field. We encourage applications from people with different backgrounds and viewpoints.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with 5.5 in each band, or equivalent when you start the course is required.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-ma-international-relations', 'MA International Relations | De Montfort University', 'MA International Relations | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 10:08:41', '2024-08-28 10:08:41'),
(1136, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MA Investigative Journalism', 'ma-investigative-journalism', '£', '17600', '500', 'Want to pursue a master\'s degree in MA Investigative Journalism in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This course is a unique partnership between DMU and Channel 4, one of the UK&rsquo;s most respected broadcasters. It&rsquo;s designed to give you the specialized skills and knowledge needed for a career in investigative video journalism.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nCreated by industry experts, the course covers important skills like deep research, handling complex data, understanding financial information, and working undercover. You&rsquo;ll also learn about media law, regulations, and ethics, and get training in investigative techniques such as using the Freedom of Information Act, data journalism, and financial journalism.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Earn an MA developed in collaboration with Channel 4, ensuring you receive industry-standard teaching from experienced academics and professional journalists.<br />\r\n- Focus on becoming an investigative video journalist with a course tailored specifically for this field.<br />\r\n- Experience different teaching styles, including traditional lectures, seminars, intensive skills workshops, news days, and studio work.<br />\r\n- In your final semester, you can independently produce an investigative journalism piece suitable for broadcast on a mainstream outlet.<br />\r\n- Learn from academics who have extensive experience as journalists, filmmakers, media consultants, and producers, helping you develop the skills needed for your career.<br />\r\n- This course is suitable for both established professionals and graduates looking to enter the field.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have a degree equivalent to a British honours degree (at least a 2:2). You should also show a strong interest in a journalism career, such as participating in student media, blogging, or broadcasting. Additionally, you should have a good understanding of current events.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Applicants should have an excellent standard of English (IELTS 6.5 or equivalent for international applicants).</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-ma-investigative-journalism', 'MA Investigative Journalism | De Montfort University', 'MA Investigative Journalism | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 10:12:29', '2024-08-28 10:12:29'),
(1137, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'LLM Criminal Justice', 'llm-criminal-justice', '£', '17950', '500', 'Want to pursue a master\'s degree in LLM Criminal Justice in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This course at De Montfort University draws on research expertise to explore how the criminal justice system works. It looks at how well the law helps victims of crime and those accused of criminal offences get justice.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou&rsquo;ll learn to critically assess different aspects of criminal law and procedures, and come up with solutions to modern problems. Through various assessments like presentations, case studies, individual exercises, report writing, and essays, you&#39;ll develop and present legal arguments with strong theoretical backing. You&rsquo;ll also gain a deeper understanding of research methods useful for a career in criminal justice.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- You&rsquo;ll be taught by experienced legal experts, including barristers, solicitors, professors, and practitioners from the international legal field.<br />\r\n- The course uses a block teaching approach, where you focus on one subject at a time with a more concentrated weekly schedule. This allows you to dive deeper into each topic and work closely with your tutors and classmates.<br />\r\n- In the &quot;Critical Issues in Sentencing and Punishment&quot; module, you&#39;ll study current sentencing policies, evaluate their theories, and assess how well they achieve justice for victims, defendants, and society.<br />\r\n- You&rsquo;ll have access to specialized learning spaces, including a crown court, a training courtroom, and a simulated Judge&#39;s Chambers suite. The Hugh Aston Building also has a dedicated law library just for law students, where you can practice scenario-based learning.<br />\r\n- You&rsquo;ll develop the values, skills, knowledge, and behaviours needed to contribute to creating a just, peaceful, and sustainable world.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Applicants should have some background knowledge in law or a related field (usually from an undergraduate degree or professional qualifications). You should typically have a degree with at least a 2:2 pass, an equivalent qualification from overseas, or a similar professional qualification. A law degree is preferred, but it&#39;s not required.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language an IELTS score of 6.5 overall with 5.5 in each band (or equivalent) when you start the course is essentially required.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-llm-criminal-justice', 'LLM Criminal Justice | De Montfort University', 'LLM Criminal Justice | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, 15, '2024-08-28 10:15:45', '2024-08-28 10:21:10'),
(1138, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'LLM Employment Law and Practice', 'llm-employment-law-and-practice', '£', '17950', '500', 'Want to pursue a master\'s degree in LLM Employment Law and Practice in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Employment law is a fascinating and quickly changing area of law that deals with important questions about work and everyday life, touching on social, political, economic, and philosophical issues. These questions often shape how employment law has developed over time.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nIn this course, you&rsquo;ll gain a deep understanding of the laws that affect HR policies and practices within a business. You&rsquo;ll also learn about the context in which your advice is needed, the potential impact your advice could have on a business, and how business decisions might be influenced by these laws.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- You will learn from experienced legal professionals, including barristers, solicitors, professors, and international legal experts. The course uses a block teaching method, which allows you to focus on one subject at a time with a more concentrated weekly schedule. This approach helps you dive deeper into each topic and work closely with your tutors and classmates.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- In the &quot;Equal Opportunities and Discrimination in the Workplace&quot; module, you&#39;ll explore equality and discrimination within social, political, and economic contexts, helping you develop practical solutions to real-world issues.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- The course will equip you with the knowledge, insights, and analytical skills to advance your career in law, business, or academia. You&#39;ll also have access to a law library in the Hugh Aston Building, exclusively for law students, with group study rooms and a quiet study area.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">-Throughout the course, you&#39;ll develop the values, skills, knowledge, and behaviours needed to contribute to a just, peaceful, and sustainable world.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Applicants are expected to have background knowledge of law or a discipline related to the LLM (usually an undergraduate degree or professional qualifications). Applicants will normally hold a degree with a minimum pass of 2:2, or equivalent.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with 5.5 in each band (or equivalent) when you start the course is essential.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-llm-employment-law-and-practice', 'LLM Employment Law and Practice | De Montfort University', 'LLM Employment Law and Practice | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 10:19:30', '2024-08-28 10:19:30'),
(1139, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'LLM International Commercial Law and Practice', 'llm-international-commercial-law-and-practice', '£', '17950', '500', 'Want to pursue a master\'s degree in LLM International Commercial Law and Practice in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This program helps you develop the skills to critically analyze key and current areas of international commercial law. Using De Montfort University&#39;s research expertise, the course explores both the theory and practice of international commercial law and evaluates how well the legal processes regulate business transactions. It also teaches you research methods specific to international commercial law.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- You will learn from legal experts, including solicitors, professors, and practitioners with specialized knowledge in employment law.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- The program uses a block teaching method, which means you focus on one subject at a time with a more concentrated weekly schedule. This allows for deeper learning and closer interaction with your tutors and classmates.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- In the &quot;International Perspectives of Company and Corporate Insolvency Law&quot; module, you can compare UK company law with European and international perspectives.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- You&#39;ll have access to specialized learning spaces, including a crown court, a training courtroom, and a simulated Judge&#39;s Chambers suite. The Hugh Aston Building also has a dedicated law library for law students, providing a space for practical, scenario-based learning.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- You will develop values, skills, knowledge, and behaviours that will help you contribute to creating a just, peaceful, and sustainable world.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Applicants are expected to have background knowledge of law or a discipline related to the LLM (usually an undergraduate degree or professional qualifications). Applicants will normally hold a degree with a minimum pass of 2:2, or equivalent.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with 5.5 in each band (or equivalent) when you start the course is essential.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-llm-international-commercial-law-and-practice', 'LLM International Commercial Law and Practice | De Montfort University', 'LLM International Commercial Law and Practice | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 10:26:25', '2024-08-28 10:26:25'),
(1140, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'LLM Medical Law Ethics and Practice', 'llm-medical-law-ethics-and-practice', '£', '17950', '500', 'Want to pursue a master\'s degree in LLM Medical Law Ethics and Practice in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This course is designed for healthcare professionals, especially those working directly with patients, including psychiatric care providers, and clinicians involved in medical research. It&rsquo;s also ideal for NHS Trust staff who focus on clinical governance, risk management, or resource allocation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThe course will help you tackle the challenges you face in today&rsquo;s workplace. Through specialized modules in medical law and ethics, you&rsquo;ll develop practical skills in the analysis, evaluation, and application of legal concepts. You&rsquo;ll learn through a mix of lectures, seminars, guided learning, independent study, problem-solving, and resource-based approaches, leading to a final assessment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Learn from legal experts, including experienced barristers, solicitors, professors, and international legal practitioners.<br />\r\n- Explore real-world ethical issues like euthanasia, abortion, mental health, medical negligence, patient safety, and Coroner&rsquo;s law.<br />\r\n- Study in dedicated legal spaces, such as a crown court that has hosted trials for centuries, a training courtroom, and a simulated Judge&#39;s Chambers suite. The university&rsquo;s Hugh Aston Building also houses a law library just for law students, perfect for hands-on learning.<br />\r\n- Develop the values, skills, and knowledge to contribute to a fairer, more peaceful, and sustainable world.<br />\r\n- Benefit from block teaching, where you focus on one subject at a time, making it easier to engage with your studies, receive regular feedback and maintain a balanced study-life routine.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Applicants should typically have a degree with at least a 2:2 pass, an equivalent qualification from another country, or a similar professional qualification. While having a law degree is preferred, it&rsquo;s not required.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an IELTS score of 6.5 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section, before starting the course.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-llm-medical-law-ethics-and-practice', 'LLM Medical Law Ethics and Practice | De Montfort University', 'LLM Medical Law Ethics and Practice | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 10:31:06', '2024-08-28 10:31:06');
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `country_id`, `university_id`, `campus_id`, `level_id`, `budget_id`, `name`, `slug`, `currency`, `fees`, `scholarship`, `description`, `overview`, `entry_requirements`, `scholarship_details`, `url`, `title`, `share_title`, `keywords`, `page_image`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1141, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'LLM SQE', 'llm-sqe', '£', '17950', '500', 'Want to pursue a master\'s degree in LLM SQE in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s SQE preparation course is carefully designed to give you the knowledge and skills needed to pass the Solicitors Qualifying Examination (SQE 1 and SQE 2), the new way to become a solicitor in England and Wales.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Access BARBRI SQE Prep software at no extra cost, which includes exam-focused workbooks, study materials, and practice exams to help you prepare. In the July SQE 1 exam, BARBRI students had a 13% higher pass rate than the average.<br />\r\n- Get personalized support from an SQE tutor, a qualified solicitor who can provide tailored career advice, help with your CV and cover letters and assist you in finding placements. These placements could count towards the two years of qualifying work experience (QWE) needed to qualify as a solicitor through the SQE route.<br />\r\n- Take advantage of the Law Mentoring Scheme, which connects you with law employers. The work experience gained through this scheme can count towards your two years of QWE and help you build important connections for your future career.<br />\r\n- Study in specialized law learning spaces, including a crown court that has been used for trials since the Middle Ages, a training courtroom, and a dedicated law library.<br />\r\n- Benefit from the support of our Advisory Board, which includes 20 leaders from local and global organizations. Law students can expect industry visits, guest lectures, mentorship, and internship opportunities.<br />\r\n- Enhance your CV through extra-curricular activities at DMU, such as DMU Street Law or the Law and Mooting Society. These activities offer chances to participate in mooting, presentations, mock trials, and interviewing.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Applicants should typically have an undergraduate law degree with at least a 2:2 pass (or an equivalent qualification). Alternatively, you can apply with an undergraduate degree in any subject, as long as you also have a Graduate Diploma in Law (GDL).</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an overall IELTS score of 6.5, with at least 5.5 in each section, before starting the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-llm-sqe', 'LLM SQE | De Montfort University', 'LLM SQE | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 10:33:53', '2024-08-28 10:33:53'),
(1142, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'LLM Sustainability Social Justice and Human Rights Law', 'llm-sustainability-social-justice-and-human-rights-law', '£', '17950', '500', 'Want to pursue a master\'s degree in LLM Sustainability Social Justice and Human Rights Law in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You will study various modules that focus on important topics like sustainability, social justice, and human rights. You&rsquo;ll explore these subjects in specific contexts and have the chance to improve your critical thinking, research, evaluation, and communication skills.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The program ends with a dissertation module, where you&rsquo;ll carry out an in-depth research project on a topic of your choice. With the guidance of a supervisor, this independent work can align with your future career goals and reflect your interests from the course.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- You&rsquo;ll learn from experienced legal experts, including barristers, solicitors, professors, and international practitioners.<br />\r\n- You&rsquo;ll develop the ability to critically assess and apply theories of human rights and social justice, considering policy objectives and the real-world demands of sustainability.<br />\r\n- You can deepen your understanding of the law in specialized learning spaces, such as a crown court that has hosted trials for centuries, a training courtroom, and a simulated Judge&#39;s Chambers suite. The university&rsquo;s Hugh Aston Building also offers a law library just for law students, perfect for hands-on learning.<br />\r\n- You&rsquo;ll build values, skills, knowledge, and behaviours that will help you contribute to creating a fairer, more peaceful, and sustainable world.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Applicants should typically have a degree with at least a 2:2 pass, or an equivalent qualification from another country, or a similar professional qualification. While a law degree is preferred, it&rsquo;s not required.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an overall IELTS score of 6.5, with at least 5.5 in each section, before starting the course.<br />\r\nScholarships</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'de-montfort-university-llm-sustainability-social-justice-and-human-rights-law', 'LLM Sustainability Social Justice and Human Rights Law | De Montfort University', 'LLM Sustainability Social Justice and Human Rights Law | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, 15, '2024-08-28 10:39:20', '2024-08-28 10:39:32'),
(1143, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'Master of Business Administration MBA (Global)', 'master-of-business-administration-mba-global', '£', '19800', '500', 'Want to study Master of Business Administration MBA (Global) in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This course focuses on building your employability and enhancing your skills. It will help you develop analytical and numerical abilities for critical thinking, problem-solving, and effective teamwork. You&rsquo;ll also learn to clearly express your skills, abilities, and achievements, creating a personal development portfolio for your CV and job applications. This makes the Global MBA course perfect for early career professionals and graduates.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- An early career MBA is ideal for recent graduates or those with little to no managerial experience.<br />\r\n- The course emphasizes developing transferable skills and helping you present your abilities and achievements in a way that stands out to employers.<br />\r\n- You&rsquo;ll have the chance to attend exclusive business talks and events, helping you build a network of industry contacts.<br />\r\n- Enjoy access to the Innovation Centre, where you can attend free events, business advice sessions, and networking opportunities, especially if you&#39;re interested in innovation or starting your own business.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Applicants should typically have an undergraduate degree in any subject with at least a 2:2 pass, or an equivalent qualification from another country, or at least 5 years of managerial work experience. Professional qualifications that are considered equivalent will also be reviewed individually.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an overall IELTS score of 6.0, with at least 5.5 in each section, before starting the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-master-of-business-administration-mba-global', 'Master of Business Administration MBA (Global) | De Montfort University', 'Master of Business Administration MBA (Global) | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 10:44:22', '2024-08-28 10:44:22'),
(1144, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MSc Mechanical Engineering', 'msc-mechanical-engineering', '£', '17600', '500', 'Want to study MSc Mechanical Engineering in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This course is designed to boost your job prospects by addressing the UK&#39;s engineering skills gap and meeting the global need for versatile engineers. It offers industry-relevant content, placement opportunities, and guidance from research-active teaching staff. As a graduate, you&rsquo;ll be ready to work on cutting-edge projects that shape the world around us.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You&rsquo;ll build your skills in core engineering areas through modules like Engineering Business Environment, Research Methods, Advanced Materials Structures and Design, and Advanced Mechanical Engineering.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Accredited by the IET*, ensuring you gain the skills and knowledge needed for an engineering career and professional registration.<br />\r\n- Learn from teaching staff who are involved in research such as combustion modelling, energy conversion, computational theology, and surface engineering.<br />\r\n- Develop practical skills in our well-equipped facilities, including labs for thermo-fluids, solid mechanics, dynamics with control, an energy lab for thermodynamics, and mechanical workshops with CNC machine tools.<br />\r\n- Join student societies like DMU Racing, where you can design and build a car to race at Silverstone and gain hands-on engineering experience.<br />\r\n- Improve your career prospects with an optional one-year placement** in your area of interest. Past students have completed placements with companies like Caterpillar and Network Rail.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have a degree similar to a British Honours degree with at least a 2:2 pass in a relevant subject. We will also consider equivalent qualifications from other countries. If you don&rsquo;t have formal academic qualifications but have extensive industry experience, we&rsquo;ll review your application individually. International students need a valid ATAS certificate to study at DMU for this course</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an overall IELTS score of 6.0, with at least 5.5 in each section, before starting the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-msc-mechanical-engineering', 'MSc Mechanical Engineering | De Montfort University', 'MSc Mechanical Engineering | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 10:48:43', '2024-08-28 10:48:43'),
(1145, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MSc Mechatronics and Robotics', 'msc-mechatronics-and-robotics', '£', '17600', '500', 'Want to study MSc in Mechatronics and Robotics in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The field of Mechatronics and Robotics is experiencing a skills shortage, which is crucial for the growth of industries in both developed and developing countries. This course will enhance your technological skills and improve your career prospects.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The program is designed to transform graduates from single-discipline backgrounds into multidisciplinary engineers ready to meet industry demands in Mechatronics and Robotics.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Accredited by The Institution of Engineering and Technology (IET)*, ensuring high-quality teaching and a recognized qualification.<br />\r\n- Mechatronic engineers are in high demand as industries seek advancements in various fields.<br />\r\n- Use our top-notch facilities, including specialized mechanical, electrical, and electronic labs, as well as spaces for making student designs.<br />\r\n- Improve your employability with a year-long work placement**, gaining valuable industry experience to boost your practical and professional skills.<br />\r\n- Our graduates have succeeded in industries like robotics, automation, manufacturing, machine vision, automotive, aerospace, material processing, and energy. They work as engineers and project managers in design, research, and product development.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have a degree similar to a British Honours degree with at least a 2:2 pass in a relevant subject. We will also consider equivalent qualifications from other countries. If you don&rsquo;t have formal academic qualifications but have significant industry experience, we will review your application individually.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an overall IELTS score of 6.0, with at least 5.5 in each section, before starting the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-msc-mechatronics-and-robotics', 'MSc Mechatronics and Robotics | De Montfort University', 'MSc Mechatronics and Robotics | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 10:52:02', '2024-08-28 10:52:02'),
(1146, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MA Music Technology and Innovation', 'ma-music-technology-and-innovation', '£', '17600', '500', 'Want to study MA Music Technology and Innovation in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s Music Technology BA is a unique and exciting course that explores new ways of creating and performing music using the latest technology. It&rsquo;s perfect for creative and innovative people who want to make exceptional music and stand out in the arts and creative industries.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You&rsquo;ll learn from internationally recognized musicians who are active performers, composers, and researchers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- The course takes place in DMU&#39;s Creative Technology Studios, where you&rsquo;ll use audio recording studios, broadcast-quality radio production studios, and management systems. You&#39;ll also have access to our Performing Arts Centre for Excellence (PACE), which includes performance spaces and a 33-channel loudspeaker system.<br />\r\n- Join a vibrant musical community with concerts, workshops, and groups like the Dirty Electronics ensemble. The university also has various student musical societies, including the Music Society, Recording Society, Sound Design Society, and DJ Society.<br />\r\n- Present your work at important cultural venues in Leicester, such as the CURVE Theatre, the Phoenix Cinema and Art Centre, and the creative hub LCB Depot.<br />\r\n- Get valuable industry experience by working with the award-winning Demon Media group, which includes Demon FM radio station and Demon TV.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You need five GCSEs at grade C or above, including English and Maths, or equivalent qualifications, plus one of the following:</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- 104 UCAS points from at least two A-levels, with Music or Music Technology at grade C or above, or<br />\r\n- A Music or Music Technology BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with grades DMM, or<br />\r\n- A pass in the QAA accredited Access to HE Music or Music Technology course with at least 15 credits in Music or Music Technology at merit. Note that you need separate GCSEs in English and Maths, as equivalency is not accepted in the Access course.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an overall IELTS score of 6.0, with at least 5.5 in each section, or an equivalent score.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-ma-music-technology-and-innovation', 'MA Music Technology and Innovation | De Montfort University', 'MA Music Technology and Innovation | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 11:07:07', '2024-08-28 11:07:07'),
(1147, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MA Pharmaceutical Biotechnology', 'ma-pharmaceutical-biotechnology', '£', '16800', '500', 'Want to study MA Pharmaceutical Biotechnology in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Pharmaceutical Biotechnology is a fast-growing area centred on developing and producing biopharmaceuticals to treat major diseases. You&#39;ll learn how to select and use systems for large-scale protein production and how to fully understand these proteins before they are applied to humans.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This course is unique because it blends theoretical knowledge with hands-on experience. You&#39;ll work on pre-clinical studies, clinical trials, and marketing, giving you a broad skill set for a career in industry or academia.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The course draws on the expertise of experienced practitioners and research-active staff, focusing on key areas like Pharmaceutical Technologies, Nanomedicine, Pharmacology, Neuroscience, and Infectious Disease research. It aligns with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals, giving you a competitive edge in the biopharmaceutical field.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- 100+ Years of Expertise: Our long-standing reputation in pharmacy teaching ensures top-quality graduates.<br />\r\n- Advanced Facilities: Develop your skills in labs with industry-standard technology, such as FACS analysis, confocal microscopes, electron microscopes, mass spectrometers, fermentation units, and tissue culture suites.<br />\r\n- Career Advancement: Graduates often move on to PhD studies or jobs in the biotech sector globally.<br />\r\n- Specialized Modules: Study various protein expression systems and stay updated with current industry practices.<br />\r\n- Business and Innovation: Learn about the business and intellectual property aspects of biotechnology, helping with career growth.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To join this course, you need at least a 2:2 or equivalent honours degree in a relevant subject such as forensic science, bioscience, pharmacy, biology, biochemistry, biotechnology, chemical engineering, microbiology, or molecular biology.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong><br />\r\nIf English isn&#39;t your first language, you must have an IELTS score of 6.5 overall, with no less than 6.0 in each part (or equivalent) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-ma-pharmaceutical-biotechnology', 'MA Pharmaceutical Biotechnology | De Montfort University', 'MA Pharmaceutical Biotechnology | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 11:47:01', '2024-08-28 11:47:01'),
(1148, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MSc Pharmaceutical Quality by Design', 'msc-pharmaceutical-quality-by-design', '£', '16800', '500', 'Want to study MSc Pharmaceutical Quality by Design in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Pharmaceutical Quality by Design (QbD) course helps you understand the challenges in creating new products for the pharmaceutical and healthcare industries. You&#39;ll learn modern methods for developing and manufacturing products that follow current best practices and QbD principles.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Our Leicester School of Pharmacy has over 100 years of experience in teaching pharmacy. This course focuses on applying global regulatory guidelines to pharmaceutical manufacturing and product development.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>- Experienced Staff: </strong>Our teachers are involved in research projects supported by Innovate UK and the Engineering and Physical Sciences Research Council.<br />\r\n<strong>- Career Preparation: </strong>The course prepares you for various careers in pharmaceuticals, including product development, manufacturing, regulatory affairs, marketing, and clinical research.<br />\r\n<strong>- Industry Connections:</strong> Strong links with the industry and guest lecturers ensure your learning is up-to-date with current practices and developments.<br />\r\n<strong>- Practical Knowledge: </strong>The course emphasizes applying QbD principles and continuous improvement to pharmaceutical product development and manufacturing.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To join this course, you need a good honours degree (at least a 2:2 or equivalent) in a science subject like chemistry, biology, chemical engineering, pharmacy, or physics.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you must have an IELTS score of 6.5 overall, with at least 6.0 in each part (or equivalent) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-msc-pharmaceutical-quality-by-design', 'MSc Pharmaceutical Quality by Design | De Montfort University', 'MSc Pharmaceutical Quality by Design | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 11:50:47', '2024-08-28 11:50:47'),
(1149, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MA Photographic History', 'ma-photographic-history', '£', '15800', '500', 'Want to study MA Photographic History in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Photography has influenced how we view the recent past and experience life today. The Photographic History MA program will teach you how to study photographic materials, practices, processes, and critical research in the field. You&rsquo;ll also gain practical skills through remote fieldwork with well-known photography organizations.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You&#39;ll learn from internationally recognized experts at the Photographic History Research Centre (PHRC), who have strong connections with major photographic collections, archives, galleries, and museums worldwide. Through research seminars, workshops, and conferences, you&rsquo;ll deepen your understanding of photography&rsquo;s relationship with history and culture, while improving your research skills and employability.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n<strong>- Flexible Study Options: </strong>Study full-time, part-time, or per-module to fit your schedule, with ongoing support from expert academic staff.<br />\r\n<strong>- Real-World Experience: </strong>Completing an independent project with a photography organization gives you practical skills and professional expertise.<br />\r\n<strong>- Focus on Culture:</strong> Explore the social and cultural impact of photography throughout history.<br />\r\n<strong>- Digital and Analogue Photography:</strong> Learn about the changing role of photography in society and its cultural significance.<br />\r\n<strong>- Expert Guidance:</strong> Work with a renowned team of scholars from the Photographic History Research Centre (PHRC) and beyond.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have a UK bachelor&rsquo;s degree with at least a 2.2 (or an equivalent qualification) in a relevant subject, such as history, museum studies, art history, photography and lens-based media, history of science, heritage studies, or literature.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an IELTS score of 6.5 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section, or an equivalent qualification, when you start the course. English language support is available through our British Council accredited Centre for English Language Learning, both before and during the course, if you need it.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'de-montfort-university-ma-photographic-history', 'MA Photographic History | De Montfort University', 'MA Photographic History | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 11:53:59', '2024-08-28 11:53:59'),
(1150, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MA Product Design', 'ma-product-design', '£', '15800', '500', 'Want to study MA Product Design in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This course is designed for students with a degree in product design, furniture design, or a related 3D design field who want to deepen their knowledge, skills, and career prospects. You&rsquo;ll gain an advanced understanding of design practice, learn about research methods, explore service design, and discover how new digital technologies can improve your work.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The flexible curriculum lets you focus on your interests and goals while equipping you with the practical skills needed for a successful career in the creative industries. Your studies will culminate in a self-directed design project, where you&rsquo;ll go through real-world product design processes like validation, prototyping, testing, and technical specifications.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n<strong>- Degree Options:</strong> Depending on your path and final project, you can earn an MA or MSc. You can also exit the course early with a Postgraduate Diploma or Certificate, based on the credits you&#39;ve earned.<br />\r\n<strong>- Career Focus: </strong>The course emphasizes employability, along with professional and commercial skills, to support your career goals&mdash;whether as a designer, entrepreneur, or in the wider creative industries.<br />\r\n<strong>- Sustainability: </strong>You&rsquo;ll learn to consider sustainability and social responsibility in every design decision, preparing you to tackle complex environmental challenges.<br />\r\n<strong>- Expert Instructors</strong>: Learn from a teaching team that is active in their fields, ensuring you acquire the most relevant skills for your career.<br />\r\n<strong>- Creative Community:</strong> Join a community working together to create new ways of thinking and redefine the future of creative practice.<br />\r\n<strong>- Work Placement:</strong> An optional year-long work placement offers valuable experience to further enhance your practical and professional skills.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have a UK bachelor&rsquo;s degree with at least a 2:2 grade in product design, furniture design, or a related subject. If you have other professional qualifications and relevant industry experience, we will review your application individually.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent), when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-ma-product-design', 'MA Product Design | De Montfort University', 'MA Product Design | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 11:58:18', '2024-08-28 11:58:18'),
(1151, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MSc Psychological Well-being', 'msc-psychological-well-being', '£', '16800', '500', 'Want to study MSc Psychological Well-being in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Mental Health and Wellbeing course helps you understand what affects mental health and wellbeing. It covers important theories and research, teaches research methods, and shows real-world practices to prepare you to make a positive impact in this field.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n<strong>- Practical Experience: </strong>Gain hands-on skills through short events where you interact with people who have lived experiences, service users, and health professionals.<br />\r\n<strong>- Therapeutic Approaches:</strong> Learn about different methods used to treat and prevent mental health issues, both traditional and modern.<br />\r\n<strong>- Psychological Theory:</strong> Develop a strong understanding of the psychological theories and research behind mental health and well-being.<br />\r\n<strong>- Wellbeing Approaches: </strong>Explore various ways to improve wellbeing, including interventions and principles that apply to different settings like work and school.<br />\r\n<strong>- Experienced Staff: </strong>Learn from experienced teachers who are both active researchers and practising psychologists.<br />\r\n<strong>- Practical Facilities: </strong>Apply what you learn in our dedicated psychology labs and research rooms with the latest technology.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You usually need a 2:2 honours degree or higher from a BPS-accredited psychology course. If you have a 2:1 honours degree in a related subject but not psychology, your application will still be considered.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.5 overall, with at least 6.0 in each section (or an equivalent), when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</span></p>', 'de-montfort-university-msc-psychological-well-being', 'MSc Psychological Well-being | De Montfort University', 'MSc Psychological Well-being | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 12:04:10', '2024-08-28 12:04:10'),
(1152, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MSc Risk Management', 'msc-risk-management', '£', '17950', '500', 'Want to study MSc Risk Management in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Risk management is important in every industry, from business and consulting to public services. Recently, there&rsquo;s been a growing recognition that managing risk is essential for shaping organizational strategy. This course is designed for those looking to start a career in risk management and for professionals who want to enhance their skills in this area.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n<strong>- Accreditation: </strong>The course is accredited by the Institute of Risk Management, and you may be able to get exemptions from their professional exams.<br />\r\n<strong>- Comprehensive Learning:</strong> You&rsquo;ll study both the numbers and the human psychology behind risky decisions.<br />\r\n<strong>- Research Opportunity:</strong> In the Dissertation in Risk Management module, you&rsquo;ll work on research in a specific area of risk management.<br />\r\n<strong>- Real-World Project:</strong> The Consultancy Project in Risk Management lets you work on a real-world project, gaining practical experience.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have an undergraduate degree in any subject with at least a 2:2 grade, or an equivalent qualification from another country, or a similar professional qualification.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you usually need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section, or an equivalent score.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-msc-risk-management', 'MSc Risk Management | De Montfort University', 'MSc Risk Management | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 12:07:26', '2024-08-28 12:07:26'),
(1153, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MSc Smart Grids and Power Systems', 'msc-smart-grids-and-power-systems', '£', '17600', '500', 'Want to study MSc Smart Grids and Power Systems in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Smart Grids &amp; Power Systems MSc course will give you a deep understanding of modern issues in electrical power systems and smart grid technology. You&rsquo;ll learn about experimental and computer modelling techniques for designing and operating smart grids, including how electricity transmission, distribution networks, and renewable energy sources work. The course also covers advanced tools for data analysis in smart grids.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n<strong>- Expert Teaching: </strong>Learn from experienced researchers and teachers with over 30 years of experience in energy and sustainable development.<br />\r\n<strong>- Specialist Facilities:</strong> Use our Smart Grid Laboratory and computer labs with industry-standard software to study power grids, renewable energy, and electric vehicle components.<br />\r\n<strong>- Career Preparation:</strong> Get ready for a career in smart grids and power engineering or take the first step towards a PhD and academic career.<br />\r\n<strong>- Work Placement: </strong>Optionally complete a year-long work placement* to gain practical experience and boost your employability.<br />\r\n<strong>- Global Experience:</strong> Enrich your studies with DMU Global&rsquo;s international opportunities and broaden your cultural perspectives.<br />\r\n<strong>- Flexible Study:</strong> Choose between full-time or part-time study to fit the course around your schedule.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have a degree equivalent to a British 2:2 honours degree in an engineering-related subject.DMU also accept similar qualifications from other countries. If you don&rsquo;t have formal qualifications but have a lot of industry experience, we will review your application individually.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section, or an equivalent score, when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-msc-smart-grids-and-power-systems', 'MSc Smart Grids and Power Systems | De Montfort University', 'MSc Smart Grids and Power Systems | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-28 12:10:43', '2024-08-28 12:10:43'),
(1154, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MSc Software Engineering', 'msc-software-engineering', '£', '18780', '500', 'Want to study MSc Software Engineering in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Our Software Engineering MSc, PG Dip, and PG Cert programs are designed with input from top companies like Airbus and Deloitte UK, ensuring that what you learn matches what the industry needs. The course is regularly updated with insights from experts at the Software Technology Research Laboratory, part of the Cyber Technology Institute, which is recognized as an &lsquo;Airbus Centre of Excellence in Cyber Security.&rsquo;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Depending on the credits you earn, you can graduate with a Postgraduate degree, Postgraduate Diploma, or Postgraduate Certificate.<br />\r\n- Study in a department known worldwide for its research and teaching in software engineering. In the latest UK Research Assessment, 85% of the research from the Software Technology Research Laboratory was rated as world-leading or internationally excellent.<br />\r\n- Access state-of-the-art labs with industry-standard software like IntelliJ, Scala, and Microsoft&rsquo;s C# and F# languages for programming.<br />\r\n- Join student groups like DMU Hackers, an ethical hacking society where you can meet others, share skills, and prepare for competitions.<br />\r\n- Enhance your career prospects with an optional one-year paid placement, allowing you to build industry contacts and gain practical experience.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have a British Honours degree with at least a 2:2 in a relevant subject. We also accept equivalent qualifications from other countries. If you don&#39;t have formal academic qualifications but have significant industry experience, we will review your application individually.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&#39;t your first language, you&#39;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent score) before starting the course.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-msc-software-engineering', 'MSc Software Engineering | De Montfort University', 'MSc Software Engineering | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-29 10:00:04', '2024-08-29 10:00:04'),
(1155, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MA Sports History and Culture', 'ma-sports-history-and-culture', '£', '15800', '500', 'Want to study MA Sports History and Culture in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Our well-established Sports History and Culture distance-learning MA provides a solid understanding of how modern sport has developed, from its traditional forms to today&#39;s practices. This program is flexible and interactive, with strong connections to the International Centre for Sports History and Culture (ICSHC), ensuring that your learning is based on the latest research.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You will explore the origins of modern sport, its cultural and global importance, and how it helps us understand society and different communities. You&#39;ll also learn how sports historians use primary sources. The course has a global focus, examining how modern sport spread from its British roots and how other countries have adapted it within their own cultures.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have a 2:2 UK bachelor&rsquo;s honours degree or higher in a relevant subject like history, other humanities, sports studies, or sociology.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an IELTS score of 6.5 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent score) before starting the course.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-ma-sports-history-and-culture', 'MA Sports History and Culture | De Montfort University', 'MA Sports History and Culture | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-29 10:03:44', '2024-08-29 10:03:44');
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `country_id`, `university_id`, `campus_id`, `level_id`, `budget_id`, `name`, `slug`, `currency`, `fees`, `scholarship`, `description`, `overview`, `entry_requirements`, `scholarship_details`, `url`, `title`, `share_title`, `keywords`, `page_image`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1156, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MSc Sustainable Built Environment', 'msc-sustainable-built-environment', '£', '17600', '500', 'Want to study MSc Sustainable Built Environment in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This program takes an interdisciplinary approach, giving students a broad understanding of energy and sustainability issues, along with an in-depth study of building physics and the modelling software used in designing modern buildings and their surroundings.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Computer modelling techniques allow students to simulate the complex interactions between buildings and their environment, both for individual buildings and on a larger urban scale. The program is modular, combining taught lessons with practical components, where students develop skills in using these techniques</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Learn from research and teaching staff who are experts in advancing knowledge and sharing their expertise.<br />\r\n- The course is accredited by the Chartered Institution of Building Services Engineers (CIBSE) and the Energy Institute (EI) until August 2024, with reaccreditation being sought from September 2024.<br />\r\n- Graduate with the knowledge and skills needed for careers in industry, the public sector, research, or education.<br />\r\n- Access specialist facilities like the Energy Laboratory, a high-tech centre for teaching, research, and technology demonstration.<br />\r\n- Graduates have gone on to work for global organizations such as the European Commission, Mott MacDonald, WSP Global, WYG, and Arup Group.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have a British Honours degree with at least a 2:2 in a relevant numerate subject, like engineering, physical sciences, or mathematics. Architects interested in computer modelling are also welcome to apply.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent score) before starting the course.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'de-montfort-university-msc-sustainable-built-environment', 'MSc Sustainable Built Environment | De Montfort University', 'MSc Sustainable Built Environment | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-29 10:06:16', '2024-08-29 10:06:16'),
(1157, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MSc Sustainable Textile Technologies', 'msc-sustainable-textile-technologies', '£', '15800', '500', 'Want to study MSc Sustainable Textile Technologies in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This course will inspire you to explore new and diverse ways to use sustainable textiles, encouraging you to push the limits of textile design and production. With support from passionate academics, you&rsquo;ll develop advanced technical skills&mdash;from design and development to construction and product testing&mdash;while critically examining the ethical and environmental impact of design. You&rsquo;ll gain a unique and innovative vision for applying textile materials.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The course is designed with industry input and constantly evolves to meet industry demands. Throughout your studies, you&rsquo;ll work closely with industry through coursework, guest talks, company trips, live projects, and competitions, providing networking opportunities and helping you develop skills that employers value.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Bring your ideas to life in our award-winning Vijay Patel building, which offers extensive facilities for textile dyeing, finishing, and printing. You&rsquo;ll also have access to one of the only university-owned, fully climate-controlled textile testing labs in the UK, where you can experiment, prototype, and test materials, products, and processes.<br />\r\n- Benefit from the expertise of the Textile Engineering and Materials (TEAM) Research Group, which contributes directly to the course content. Their research covers areas like textile processing, biodegradable and compostable textiles, healthcare textiles, performance textiles, and sustainable practices.<br />\r\n- Showcase your work in DMU&rsquo;s The Gallery, which attracts industry visitors and the public, or at Leicester&rsquo;s LCB Depot during Fashion Season, where you can present your final-term work.<br />\r\n- Learn from our experienced teaching team and skilled technicians, who have vast industry experience and can provide expert guidance in garment and product technology, textile innovation, fabric construction, and sustainable practices.<br />\r\n- Enhance your studies with an optional year-long work placement, gaining valuable practical and professional skills. Past students have taken on diverse roles, from Fashion Designer in Residence at Heathfield School, Ascot, to Quality Administrator at Baltex, Nottingham, a leading supplier of high-performance technical textiles.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have a 2:2 UK bachelor&rsquo;s honours degree or higher in a fashion or textile-related subject, management, business, art, design, or a related science, engineering, or social science field.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent score) before starting the course.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'de-montfort-university-msc-sustainable-textile-technologies', 'MSc Sustainable Textile Technologies | De Montfort University', 'MSc Sustainable Textile Technologies | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-29 10:08:43', '2024-08-29 10:08:43'),
(1158, 2, 12, 6, 5, 5, 'MA Theatre and Performance', 'ma-theatre-and-performance', '£', '15800', '500', 'Want to study MA Theatre and Performance in the UK? Let’s check the scholarships and entry requirements', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This course focuses on supporting original work that connects with today&rsquo;s audience and our current experiences. It also looks at the history and practices of both popular and experimental theatre to help understand the future of these fields.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The team has expertise in areas such as creating new work, performer training, live art, popular theatre, immersive and interactive theatre, documentation, writing for performance, and more. Collaboration and interdisciplinary work are central to the course, and you&rsquo;re encouraged to join in various extra-curricular and creative activities at DMU.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Depending on the credits you earn, you can complete the course with a Postgraduate Diploma or Postgraduate Certificate.<br />\r\n- Study different theatre and performance practices and their contexts to develop your skills and interests.<br />\r\n- Learn from internationally recognized staff who are active artists and scholars, exploring creative, critical, and conceptual ideas.<br />\r\n- Benefit from DMU&rsquo;s status as a Centre for Excellence in Performance Arts, with excellent facilities, including specialist studios and rehearsal spaces for theatre and performance.<br />\r\n- Get opportunities to work with industry professionals and artists through our local, national, and international connections.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You should have a 2:2 UK bachelor&rsquo;s honours degree or higher in a related subject, like Drama, Performing Arts, Theatre Arts, or Visual Arts. If you have other professional qualifications or industry experience, we will review your application individually.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent score) before starting the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-ma-theatre-and-performance', 'MA Theatre and Performance | De Montfort University', 'MA Theatre and Performance | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-08-29 10:11:19', '2024-08-29 10:11:19'),
