(1318, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Business Management', 'ba-hons-business-management', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Business Management in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Watch Dr. Irina Gokh discuss the exciting opportunities available to DMU&rsquo;s students.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This practical course is designed to prepare you for the future, covering growing fields like artificial intelligence. You&#39;ll study various business areas that adapt to the changing market, including modules like Digital Transformation and Innovation in Business, and Ethical and Responsible Leadership.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Employability is central to our Business Management course. You&#39;ll have the chance to take a year-long placement and work on real-world case studies, getting insights from global brands like Apple and Amazon. You&#39;ll move beyond textbooks to apply your knowledge through business simulations set by executives from these top companies.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You&#39;ll receive a strong foundation in business management, including key areas like accounting, economics, finance, human resource management, marketing, and sustainability.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Get hands-on experience with global companies through case studies and business simulations with brands like Amazon and Apple.<br />\r\n- Attend guest lectures from top companies, including Amazon and Apple, and learn from industry experts.<br />\r\n- Gain a thorough understanding of business management, including evaluating organizations and their operations.<br />\r\n- Develop skills and values to contribute to a fair and sustainable world through the Contemporary Issues in Sustainable Business module.<br />\r\n- Secure year-long placements with companies like BMW, Jaguar Land Rover, and Siemens, with support from our Careers Team.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>GCSEs</strong><br />\r\n- You need five GCSEs at grade 4 or above, including English and Maths.<br />\r\n<strong>Plus one of the following:</strong><br />\r\n- A Levels: Typically, you need 112 UCAS points from at least two A-Level subjects or equivalent (like BTEC).<br />\r\n- T Levels: You need a Merit grade.<br />\r\n<strong>BTEC:</strong><br />\r\n- BTEC National Diploma: Distinction/Distinction/Merit<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma: Distinction/Distinction/Merit</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Alternative Qualifications:</strong><br />\r\nAccess to HE Diploma: Pass with a total of 112 UCAS tariff points, including at least 30 Level 3 credits at Merit. English and Maths GCSEs are required separately; they can&#39;t be included in the Access qualification. It&rsquo;s usually expected that students have had a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\nInternational Baccalaureate: 26 or more points.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with at least 5.5 in each part (or an equivalent test).</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-ba-hons-business-management', 'BA (Hons) Business Management | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Business Management | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-02 09:42:18', '2024-09-02 09:42:18'),
(1319, 2, 12, 6, 6, 8, 'BSc (Hons) Computer Games Programming', 'bsc-hons-computer-games-programming', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BSc (Hons) Computer Games Programming in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p>Jethro Shell, Senior Lecturer, discusses the benefits of studying Computer Games Programming at DMU. The computer games industry is growing rapidly, now worth more than twice as much as it was in 2007, offering many career opportunities for graduates.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\nThis course helps you turn your passion for computer games into a career. You&#39;ll learn the latest techniques for developing games for different platforms, including web and mobile, and get hands-on experience with game design and programming languages.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features</strong><br />\r\n- Use popular game development software like Unity3D and Unreal Engine.<br />\r\n- Join our Game Society or E-Sports Society to enhance your experience by playing games, attending events, and competing in tournaments. You can also collaborate with Game Art students in game jams.<br />\r\n- Gain real-world experience with a placement year. Previous students have worked as Software Engineers and Programmers for companies like Virtual Arts.<br />\r\n- Get international exposure through our DMU Global programme, with opportunities to visit top tech companies in places like San Francisco and New York.<br />\r\n- The course is certified by the British Computer Society (BCS), ensuring it meets high industry standards.</p>', '<p><strong>Typical Entry Requirements</strong><br />\r\n- A Levels: 112 UCAS points from at least two A-levels.<br />\r\n- BTEC: National Diploma or Extended Diploma with grades DMM.<br />\r\n- GCSEs: Five GCSEs at grade 4 or above, including English and Maths.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Alternative Qualifications</strong><br />\r\n- Access to HE: Pass the QAA-accredited Access to HE course, with separate GCSEs in English and Maths required. Students usually need to have had a break from full-time education before taking this course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26 or more points.<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>English Langauge Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section, or an equivalent score. English language support is available through our British Council-accredited Centre for English Language Learning, both before and during the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-bsc-hons-computer-games-programming', 'BSc (Hons) Computer Games Programming | De Montfort University', 'BSc (Hons) Computer Games Programming | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-02 09:48:29', '2024-09-02 09:48:29'),
