(1362, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BSc (Hons) Computer Networks and Security', 'bsc-hons-computer-networks-and-security', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BSc (Hons) Computer Networks and Security in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This degree program is designed to prepare graduates who can meet the growing need for expertise in computer networks, security, and programming, driven by the rise of Next-Generation Network (NGN) services like VoIP and advanced network models such as SDN and NFV, where network devices are now programmable virtual entities in the cloud.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Alongside core modules in computer science and cyber security, the course includes key networking modules that align with the new Cisco certification path, developed in partnership with Cisco. These modules are focused on industry needs and are geared towards certifications, ensuring graduates have the skills required for high employability.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- You will join the Cisco Networking Academy, covering the content of three Cisco certifications: Cisco Certified Network Associate, Cisco CyberOps Associate, and Cisco DevNet Associate, plus an additional course in Network Security.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Free Cisco assessments for relevant modules will give you a Course Completion Certificate/Digital Badge from Cisco Networking Academy, verifying your skills and preparing you to pursue commercial certifications at a third-party exam centre.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- With over 50 years of computing experience, you&#39;ll benefit from a wealth of research and academic expertise to support your learning.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- The course is taught by experts from DMU&rsquo;s Cyber Technology Institute, which has an international reputation in cyber security and has influenced the approach of the UK government and leading organizations.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- DMU has been recognized as a gold standard &#39;Academic Centre of Excellence in Cyber Security Education&#39; by the UK&#39;s National Cyber Security Centre (NCSC), part of GCHQ, making it the first university in the East Midlands to earn this prestigious status.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A typical offer requires 112 UCAS points from at least two A-levels or equivalent or a BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with a grade of DMM. You also need five GCSEs at grade 4 or higher, including English and Mathematics, or equivalent qualifications.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Other accepted qualifications include:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- A pass in a QAA-accredited Access to HE course, but you still need separate GCSEs in English and Mathematics, as these are not covered by the Access course.<br />\r\n- You usually need to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>You can also apply with:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- An International Baccalaureate score of 26 or more points.<br />\r\n- A T Level with a Merit grade.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you must have an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section, or an equivalent score, when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-bsc-hons-computer-networks-and-security', 'BSc (Hons) Computer Networks and Security | De Montfort University', 'BSc (Hons) Computer Networks and Security | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, 15, '2024-09-03 06:10:29', '2024-09-03 06:20:55'),
(1363, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BSc (Hons) Computer Science', 'bsc-hons-computer-science', '£', '16250', NULL, 'Want to study BSc (Hons) Computer Science in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">From programming to software engineering, computer science connects to many industries, including medicine, education, entertainment, security, and architecture.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Find your place in this diverse course at DMU. With over 50 years of teaching experience and BCS accreditation, we focus on modern approaches to developing software systems and exploring both theoretical and practical programming concepts and software design methods.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Our facilities offer computer workstations for students, with four connected labs equipped with HP PCs running Windows and Linux. Many of the software packages are open source, so students can download and use them at home as needed for their course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU welcome applicants from various backgrounds.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>You need:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Five GCSEs at grade 4 or higher, including English and Maths.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Plus one of the following:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- A typical offer is 112 UCAS points, with at least two A Levels or equivalent (e.g., BTEC).<br />\r\n- T Levels with a Merit grade.<br />\r\n- BTEC National Diploma with Distinction/Distinction/Merit.<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with Distinction/Distinction/Merit.<br />\r\n- Five GCSEs at grade C or above, including English, or an equivalent qualification.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Other accepted qualifications include:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- A pass in a QAA-accredited Access to HE course with a total of 112 UCAS points, including at least 30 Level 3 credits at Merit. Separate GCSEs in English and Maths are required, as equivalency is not accepted within the Access qualification. Usually, you need to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- An International Baccalaureate with 26 or more points.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong><br />\r\nIf English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section, or an equivalent score, when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-bsc-hons-computer-science', 'BSc (Hons) Computer Science | De Montfort University', 'BSc (Hons) Computer Science | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-03 06:16:40', '2024-09-03 06:16:40'),
(1364, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Concept and Comic Arts', 'ba-hons-concept-and-comic-arts', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Concept and Comic Arts in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This course covers two main areas: concept art and comic art, both focusing on essential traditional art skills and modern digital techniques.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In concept art, you&#39;ll learn to master tools and techniques used in the industry to create art for film and video games, from pre-production to post-production. In comic art, you&#39;ll gain practical skills in generating ideas, visual storytelling, and visual communication.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">These two areas open up a wide range of creative opportunities for you. Your learning will be supported by studying the historical, cultural, and social contexts of print and web-based comics, graphic novels, and visual communication, which will enhance your understanding and practice.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou need 112 UCAS points from at least two A-levels, with Art and Design at grade B or higher, or an Art and Design BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with a grade of DDM. You also need five GCSEs at grade 4 or higher, including English and Maths, or equivalent qualifications.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Other accepted qualifications include:</strong><br />\r\n- A pass in a QAA-accredited Access to HE Art and Design course, with at least 15 level-3 credits in Art and Design at Distinction. You still need a separate GCSE in English.<br />\r\n- A pass in an Art and Design Foundation Diploma.<br />\r\n-Typically, you should have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>You can also apply with:</strong><br />\r\n- An International Baccalaureate score of 30 or more points, including Art and Design at a higher level with a grade of 6.<br />\r\n- A T Level with a Merit grade.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong><br />\r\nIf English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section, or an equivalent score, when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-ba-hons-concept-and-comic-arts', 'BA (Hons) Concept and Comic Arts | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Concept and Comic Arts | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-03 06:23:54', '2024-09-03 06:23:54'),
(1365, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Creative Writing', 'ba-hons-creative-writing', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Creative Writing in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We welcome students who are passionate about creative writing, eager to build on their current strengths, and excited to develop new ones. You&#39;ll learn from successful published writers and become part of a creative and supportive community of writers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s program is hands-on, meaning you&rsquo;ll learn by doing. Workshops involve working together, giving and receiving feedback, drafting, revising, and thinking critically about your work. The curriculum includes industry-focused skills to help you become a confident writer who can professionally promote, present, and publish your work.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- You can choose to focus on Drama, Education, English Literature, Film, History, Journalism, or Media as part of this degree.<br />\r\n- Learn from successful published writers and join a creative community of passionate writers.<br />\r\n- The program is uniquely organized by theme and helps you develop skills in various writing styles, such as fiction, poetry, memoir, screenwriting, and digital writing.<br />\r\n- DMU encourages you to join local writing networks, take part in spoken word events, and share and publish your work through book fairs and festivals, including DMU&#39;s annual States of Independence book festival.</p>', '<p>You need 104 points from at least two A-levels, a BTEC Extended Diploma with a DMM grade, or an International Baccalaureate with 24 or more points. T Levels with a Merit grade are also accepted.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>You also need five GCSEs with grades 9-4, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or higher.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Other accepted qualifications include:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>- A pass in an Access course with 30 Level 3 credits at Merit or higher, plus GCSE English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or higher. Usually, you should have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- A BTEC First Diploma plus two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or higher.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section, or an equivalent score when you start the course.</p>', '<p>Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'de-montfort-university-ba-hons-creative-writing', 'BA (Hons) Creative Writing | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Creative Writing | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-03 06:27:44', '2024-09-03 06:27:44'),
