(1588, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Criminology', 'ba-hons-criminology', '£', '15750', '2000', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'null', 'BA (Hons) Criminology | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Criminology | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-09 06:48:18', '2024-09-09 06:48:18'),
(1589, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Criminology with Psychology', 'ba-hons-criminology-with-psychology', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Criminology with Psychology in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Criminology with Psychology degree looks at the causes of crime, the legal system, and how society responds to crime, along with the study of psychology.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">It gives students practical knowledge and useful skills to help them think critically about society&#39;s systems and work towards creating a fairer community. The focus is mainly on the sociology of crime, with insights from psychology, philosophy, social policy, and law. This helps students understand current issues in criminology both locally and globally and develop a well-rounded view of criminal justice.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students will gain personal and professional skills that improve job prospects, such as critical thinking, ethics, and professional conduct, along with theoretical and practical skills for careers in criminal and social justice.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Learn from a team of criminologists who are actively involved in teaching and research, many of whom have worked in criminal justice and are connected to groups like the British Society of Criminology.<br />\r\n- Study a wide range of topics through engaging, hands-on learning methods.<br />\r\n- Build skills that will improve your employability when you finish the course.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n- Learn from experienced academics who focus on global issues and work towards promoting Peace, Justice, and Stronger Institutions (SDG16), for which DMU is the global hub.<br />\r\n- Take part in exciting learning experiences through DMU Global, with past trips to places like Auschwitz to study state crime, Chicago to explore subcultures, and Bosnia and Herzegovina to learn about genocide education.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>GCSEs: </strong>You need five GCSEs at grade C/4 or higher, including English.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Plus one of the following:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>A Levels:</strong> At least 112 points from two or more A levels.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>T Levels: </strong>Merit grade.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>BTEC</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- BTEC National Diploma: Distinction/Merit/Merit<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma: Distinction/Merit/Merit</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Access to HE Diploma</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Pass an Access to HE course with 112 UCAS points, including at least 30 Level 3 credits at Merit. Students usually need to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>International Baccalaureate</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">24+ points.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an overall IELTS score of 6.5, with at least 5.5 in each section, before starting the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Criminology with Psychology | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Criminology with Psychology | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-09 06:56:29', '2024-09-09 06:56:29'),
(1590, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BSc (Hons) Cyber Security', 'bsc-hons-cyber-security', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BSc (Hons) Cyber Security in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Technology and computer systems are a big part of our daily lives, and keeping the data they store safe is very important. With many businesses seeing online security as a top priority, there is a growing demand for cybersecurity professionals.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In our Cyber Security BSc course, you will learn about different types of cyber-attacks, how to stop them, and how to prevent them in the future. You&#39;ll explore how to create highly secure software and systems, conduct thorough penetration testing, and study cryptography (the science of securing information). By thinking like a hacker, you&#39;ll develop strong problem-solving skills that are highly valued in the workplace.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Throughout the course, you&#39;ll build key computing and cyber security skills, including the basics of computing, secure coding, and computer ethics. In your third year, you&#39;ll complete a Final Project, where you&#39;ll creatively solve a real-world problem for a business or society.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A typical offer is 112 UCAS points from at least two A-levels or a BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with grades of DMM, plus: Five GCSEs at grade 4 or above, including English and Maths.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nOther accepted qualifications:<br />\r\n- Pass an Access to HE course (QAA accredited). You&rsquo;ll still need separate GCSEs in English and Maths, as the Access course doesn&#39;t count for these.<br />\r\n- Students usually need to take a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26+ points.<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit grade.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your basic language, an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with 5.5 in each band (or equivalent) when you start the course is essential.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'null', 'BSc (Hons) Cyber Security | De Montfort University', 'BSc (Hons) Cyber Security | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-09 07:03:04', '2024-09-09 07:03:04'),
