(2084, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) English Literature', 'ba-hons-english-literature', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) English Literature in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Study a wide range of literature in English, from writers around the world. Explore topics like novels, Victorian and Romantic literature, Shakespeare, text technologies, and modernism. Learn how books and texts work and discuss how literature impacts society today and in the past. You&#39;ll also develop skills in critical thinking, creativity, and research. You can choose to focus on areas like Creative Writing, Drama, Education, English Language, Film, History, Journalism, or Media as part of your degree.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nBy studying English Literature at DMU, you&rsquo;ll join a supportive and friendly academic community that is passionate about literature. You&rsquo;ll learn from top experts in the field and be encouraged to express your ideas confidently and write with clarity.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features</strong><br />\r\n- Learn from top academics and guest speakers, including well-known writers like Kate Forsyth and Carol Ann Duffy.<br />\r\n- Choose a focus area like Creative Writing, Drama, Education, Film, History, Journalism, or Media. These options will enrich your studies and open up more career opportunities after graduation.<br />\r\nIn 2022, 90% of students were satisfied with the course (National Student Survey).<br />\r\n- Explore both print and digital humanities. You can use a traditional hand printing press or learn programming languages like HTML to create and study texts through the Centre for Textual Studies.<br />\r\n- Enjoy dynamic learning with a mix of teaching styles and assessment methods to develop a wide range of skills.<br />\r\n- Get hands-on experience through placements and internships. Previous students have worked with the National Space Centre, Age Concern, the Leicester Mercury, and local schools.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- 112 points from at least 2 A-levels<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with DMM<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26+ points<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit<br />\r\n- Plus, five GCSEs (grades 9-4) including English Language or Literature with a grade of 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For those taking an Access course, you&rsquo;ll need to pass with 30 level 3 credits at Merit and have GCSE English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or above. Typically, students need to have had a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nWe also accept the BTEC First Diploma, along with two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&#39;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with 5.5 in each band (or equivalent), by the time you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) English Literature | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) English Literature | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 06:51:52', '2024-09-14 06:51:52'),
(2085, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) English Literature with Mandarin', 'ba-hons-english-literature-with-mandarin', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) English Literature with Mandarin in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Study a wide variety of English literature from writers around the world and different periods, like Victorian and Romantic literature, as well as famous authors like William Shakespeare and Jane Austen. You&#39;ll learn how to analyze texts and explore literature&#39;s role in society, both today and throughout history. You&#39;ll be taught by experienced academics who will help you express your ideas clearly and write with confidence and skill.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nIn addition to English literature, you will also study Mandarin at either a beginner or post-beginner level. This will help you improve your language skills and give you insights into China&#39;s culture, history, politics, and art.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nBy studying English Literature with Mandarin at DMU, you&#39;ll become part of a friendly and supportive academic community. Graduates from this course go on to work in various fields, including media, marketing, publishing, teaching, public relations, and government jobs.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- Learn Mandarin while studying English poetry, novels, and plays from different periods and regions, with the option to focus on what interests you the most.<br />\r\n- Be taught by top academics who do leading research in areas like medieval to modern literature, language, creative writing, and digital studies.<br />\r\n- Stand out by gaining recognized skills in Mandarin. Study at your own pace while learning about Chinese society, culture, and people.<br />\r\n- Build practical skills through internships and work placements. Students have previously worked at places like the National Space Centre, the Leicester Mercury newspaper, and local schools and charities.<br />\r\n- Enjoy a variety of teaching styles and assessments that keep your learning fresh and help you develop a wide range of skills.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Typical entry requirements:</strong><br />\r\n- 112 points from at least two A-levels<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with DMM<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26+ points<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit<br />\r\n-Plus five GCSEs in grades 9-4, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>For Access students:</strong><br />\r\n- Pass with 30 level 3 credits at Merit, plus GCSE English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or above.<br />\r\n- Students should usually have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- We also accept the BTEC First Diploma plus two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you will need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent score), when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) English Literature with Mandarin | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) English Literature with Mandarin | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 06:57:08', '2024-09-14 06:57:08'),
(2086, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Esports Production', 'ba-hons-esports-production', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Esports Production in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Please note that we are not accepting applications for this course for September 2024. You might want to check out our Media Production BSc course instead.<br />\r\nEsports is one of the fastest-growing areas in the creative industry, and it&#39;s expected to bring in &pound;4.4 billion globally by 2027. With a focus on live events, broadcasting, streaming, and content creation, now is an exciting time to get involved.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThe Esports Production BA (Hons) gives you a broad education in esports, helping you prepare for various roles in this fast-paced industry. You&rsquo;ll start by exploring the cultures and history of gaming and esports, then move on to practical skills in event production, data analysis, and broadcasting technology. Each year, you&rsquo;ll work on a live esports event that you design yourself.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key features:</strong><br />\r\n- Use our top-notch facilities, like our Creative Technology Studios, which have audio recording rooms, broadcast-standard radio studios, multi-camera TV setups, and green screens.<br />\r\n- Benefit from the expertise at Leicester Media School, where the teaching staff have years of experience in broadcasting and still work in the industry.<br />\r\n- Take part in DMU Global, which offers chances to travel and grow. Past students have visited places like Berlin to learn about its media history and gone behind the scenes at NBC in New York.<br />\r\n- Boost your career with a work placement. DMU&rsquo;s Careers Team can help you find placements with industry leaders or local businesses, with many offering paid opportunities.<br />\r\n- Join the DMU Esports Society to compete in UK and international leagues like NUEL and NSE. The Society supports a wide range of games such as League of Legends, Overwatch, Valorant, Rocket League, and more.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- You will usually need 104 UCAS points from at least two A-levels or a BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with a DMM grade. You also need five GCSEs at grade 4 or above, including English (or an equivalent qualification).</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Other qualifications accepted:</strong><br />\r\n- A pass in a QAA-accredited Access to HE course, but you must have a separate GCSE in English, as Access does not count for this. We usually expect students to have taken a break from full-time education before starting an Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 24+ points.<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit grade.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Langauge Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent score) when you start the course. English language support is available through our British Council-accredited Centre for English Language Learning, both before and during the course if needed.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Esports Production | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Esports Production | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 07:01:33', '2024-09-14 07:01:33'),
(2087, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BSc (Hons) Fashion Business', 'bsc-hons-fashion-business', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BSc (Hons) Fashion Business in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The fashion world is changing quickly with new technology, global trends, and shifts in what consumers want. Now is a great time to study Fashion Business.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this course, you&#39;ll learn about fashion business models, marketing, buying, and data analysis. You&#39;ll also focus on digital changes, sustainability, and ethical business practices.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s award-winning facilities offer hands-on learning in textile labs, making this Fashion Business course unique. You can even switch to the Fashion Buying with Marketing or Merchandising course after the first year. Our expert staff will support you with strong tutoring and a network of opportunities.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You&rsquo;ll connect with industry groups like the Association of Suppliers to the British Clothing Industry (ASBCI) and the Association for Fashion Business Employability (AFBE), helping you build skills, confidence, and professional connections.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You&rsquo;ll also learn about fashion finance, including budgeting, sales forecasts, and planning. Plus, you&#39;ll develop key merchandising skills such as range building, sales forecasting, and presentation.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>DMU welcome applicants from different backgrounds. Here&rsquo;s what you need to apply:</strong><br />\r\n- Art and Design Foundation course or<br />\r\n- 112 UCAS points from at least 2 A-levels<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with grades DMM<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26+ points or<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Plus:</strong><br />\r\n- Five GCSEs with grades 9-4, including English Language or Literature, and Maths at grade 4 or above.<br />\r\n<strong>Or:</strong><br />\r\n- Access course: Pass with 30 Level 3 credits at Merit and GCSEs in English (Language or Literature) and Maths at grade 4 or above. Usually, we need students to have taken a break from full-time education before doing the Access course.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>We also accept:</strong><br />\r\n- BTEC First Diploma plus two GCSEs including English Language, Literature, and Maths at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nIf English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section, or an equivalent score when you start the course.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If you need extra help with English, our British Council-accredited Centre for English Language Learning offers tuition before and during the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BSc (Hons) Fashion Business | De Montfort University', 'BSc (Hons) Fashion Business | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 07:07:51', '2024-09-14 07:07:51'),
(2088, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Fashion Buying with Design', 'ba-hons-fashion-buying-with-design', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Fashion Buying with Design in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Explore the exciting world of fashion with this hands-on course. You&#39;ll learn about trend analysis, design, retail management, and supply chain logistics. You&#39;ll also get to work with industry experts, visit fashion companies, and gain real-world buying experience to kickstart your career.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s supportive teachers will help you every step of the way, making sure you have the resources and guidance to succeed. You&#39;ll develop your design skills, create garments, and bring your ideas to life through pattern-making, sewing workshops, and 3D digital design.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU accept students from various backgrounds. To apply, you need:<br />\r\n- An Art and Design Foundation course, or<br />\r\n- 112 points from at least 2 A levels, or<br />\r\n- A BTEC Extended Diploma with DMM, or<br />\r\n- An International Baccalaureate with 26+ points, or<br />\r\n- T Levels with Merit, plus<br />\r\n- Five GCSEs graded 9-4, including English Language or Literature and Maths at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Other qualifications we accept:</strong><br />\r\n- Pass in an Access course with 30 Level 3 credits at Merit, plus GCSE English (Language or Literature) and Maths at grade 4 or above. We usually need students to have had a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- A BTEC First Diploma plus two GCSEs including English Language, Literature, and Maths at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Langauge Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with 5.5 in each band (or equivalent) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Buying with Design | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Buying with Design | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 08:56:49', '2024-09-14 08:56:49');
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `country_id`, `university_id`, `campus_id`, `level_id`, `budget_id`, `name`, `slug`, `currency`, `fees`, `scholarship`, `description`, `overview`, `entry_requirements`, `scholarship_details`, `url`, `title`, `share_title`, `keywords`, `page_image`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(2089, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Fashion Buying with Marketing', 'ba-hons-fashion-buying-with-marketing', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Fashion Buying with Marketing with Design in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Fashion buying needs both business sense and theoretical knowledge. You&#39;ll learn about the roles and duties of fashion buyers, from creating designs to selling products. The focus will be on the business side of fashion, including planning, branding, public relations, and using social media.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You will use computer-aided design (CAD) to present your design and marketing ideas professionally. You&#39;ll also work on writing reports, selecting data, and presenting and analyzing information.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You&#39;ll gain practical skills to tackle the challenges of the fashion industry, especially as more consumers shop online instead of in stores. Emphasis will be on sustainability and social responsibility, helping you drive innovation throughout the buying process.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Work on real projects with industry partners and learn from buying marketing, and design experts. Past projects have included collaborations with brands like Curvy Kate, Next, and Joules.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Learn to analyze consumer behaviour to create effective marketing and promotional campaigns for retailers. Boost your career with a year-long placement. Previous students have worked with companies like Next, Urban Outfitters, Mamas &amp; Papas, Joules, Yours Clothing, and O&rsquo;Neill.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Graduates have found jobs at companies such as Reiss, Next, Marks &amp; Spencer, River Island, and Selfridges, or have started their successful businesses.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU welcome applicants from different backgrounds.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>You can apply if you have:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- An Art and Design Foundation course<br />\r\n- 112 UCAS points from at least 2 A-levels<br />\r\n- A BTEC Extended Diploma with DMM grades<br />\r\n- An International Baccalaureate with 26+ points<br />\r\n- T Levels with a Merit grade</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You also need five GCSEs graded 9-4, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Alternative qualifications we accept include:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- An Access course with 30 Level 3 credits at Merit and GCSE English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or above. We usually require you to have had a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- The BTEC First Diploma plus two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent score) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Buying with Marketing | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Buying with Marketing | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 09:02:33', '2024-09-14 09:02:33'),
(2090, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Fashion Buying with Merchandising', 'ba-hons-fashion-buying-with-merchandising', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Fashion Buying with Merchandising in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Get a deep understanding of how buying in fashion works, including trading, reacting to sales, and managing promotions. The merchandising part of the course focuses on the numbers behind choosing and managing fashion products and stock.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We&rsquo;ll help you build your skills through personal development, research, and critical thinking. We emphasize sustainability and social responsibility, so you&#39;ll graduate ready to bring new ideas to every stage of the buying process.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The fashion industry is changing, with more focus on online shopping. We work with industry professionals to make sure your learning is relevant and to help you adapt to the fast-paced fashion world.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You&rsquo;ll learn essential skills for a career in fashion buying, including communication and business knowledge. You&rsquo;ll also get insights from fashion experts to prepare you for roles in merchandising or related fields.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Understand fashion finance, including budgets, forecasts, and sales analysis. Develop skills in merchandising, such as range building, sales forecasting, and critical path management.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU welcome applicants from different backgrounds.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>You can apply if you have:</strong><br />\r\n- An Art and Design Foundation course, or<br />\r\n- At least 112 UCAS points from 2 A-levels, or<br />\r\n- A BTEC Extended Diploma with grades DMM, or<br />\r\n- An International Baccalaureate with 26+ points, or<br />\r\n- T Levels with a Merit grade.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You also need five GCSEs in grades 9-4, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or higher, and Maths at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Alternative qualifications include:</strong><br />\r\n- An Access to Higher Education course with 30 Level 3 credits at Merit and GCSE English (Language or Literature) and Maths at grade 4 or above. We usually expect students to have had a break from full-time education before starting this course.<br />\r\n- A BTEC First Diploma plus two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent test) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Buying with Merchandising | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Buying with Merchandising | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, 15, '2024-09-14 09:10:20', '2024-09-14 09:11:07'),
(2091, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Fashion Communication and Styling', 'ba-hons-fashion-communication-and-styling', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Fashion Communication and Styling in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In the global fashion industry, fashion stylists and communicators create visual stories and use technology and promotional platforms to showcase fashion. You&rsquo;ll learn how to connect with audiences and turn fashion products into trendy must-haves.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You&rsquo;ll get good at visual research, illustration, storyboarding, and managing projects. During your studies, you&rsquo;ll work with classmates and industry professionals, building a network of contacts and opportunities for your future career.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU accept students from different backgrounds.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>You need one of the following:</strong><br />\r\n- Art and Design Foundation<br />\r\n- 112 UCAS points from at least 2 A-levels<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with DMM grades<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate with 26+ points<br />\r\n- T Levels with Merit</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Plus, you need five GCSEs with grades 9-4, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If you have an Access to HE Diploma, you need 30 Level 3 credits at Merit and GCSE English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or above. Usually, we prefer that you&rsquo;ve had a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\nDMU also accept the BTEC First Diploma plus two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with 5.5 in each band (or an equivalent score) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Communication and Styling | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Communication and Styling | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 09:17:08', '2024-09-14 09:17:08'),
(2092, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Fashion Design', 'ba-hons-fashion-design', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Fashion Design in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s Fashion Design students get to use professional-level facilities and work with well-known industry brands like the British Fashion Council, Burberry, Warehouse, and New Look.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You can specialize in menswear, womenswear, or fashion knitwear while learning subjects like fashion illustration, creative concept development, pattern cutting, and computer-aided design (CAD). Sustainability is a big focus, and students have worked with researchers on projects like zero-waste pattern cutting and fabric repurposing.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Many of our talented graduates have recently showcased their collections at fashion weeks and events across the UK and in cities like Shanghai, Dubai, and Hong Kong.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>DMU accept applicants from different backgrounds.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Art and Design Foundation or<br />\r\n- 104 UCAS points from at least 2 A-levels<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with DMM<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26+ points or<br />\r\n- T Levels with Merit<br />\r\n- Plus, five GCSEs at grades 9-4, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For Access courses, you need 30 Level 3 credits at Merit and GCSE English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or above. Usually, students must have taken a break from full-time education before starting an Access course.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU also accept the BTEC First Diploma plus two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you will need an overall IELTS score of 6.0 with at least 5.5 in each part when you begin the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Design | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Design | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 09:25:52', '2024-09-14 09:25:52'),
(2093, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Fashion Management (Level 6 Top Up)', 'ba-hons-fashion-management-level-6-top-up', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Fashion Management (Level 6 Top Up) in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><meta charset=\"utf-8\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Unlock your creative potential in Fashion Management and learn the essential skills needed for a career in this exciting industry.</p>\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThis top-up program is for students who have completed Level 5 education, such as an HND (Level 5) in the UK or an equivalent international qualification in Art &amp; Design or Business. It allows you to earn a BA (Honours) in Fashion Management in just one year.</p>\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThe program focuses on fashion business and management, teaching you about fashion buying, marketing, innovation, and entrepreneurship. You&rsquo;ll learn how to manage the product development process from the initial idea to the point of sale. The course ends with a major research project, where you can focus on Marketing, Management, Buying, or Trends based on your interests.</p>\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nAfter completing this course, you can move on to Fashion Management with a Marketing MA at DMU, earning two degrees in two years.</p>\r\n\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key areas of study include:</strong><br />\r\n- Understanding fashion business and management, including product innovation, intellectual property law, business planning, and entrepreneurship.<br />\r\n- Developing buying skills like range planning, building, negotiation, and analysis to create profitable fashion collections.<br />\r\n- Exploring modern issues in the global fashion market, such as consumer behaviour, market segmentation, and fashion promotion (both online and offline).<br />\r\n- Learning entrepreneurial skills and how to write a business plan, covering marketing strategies, product launches, and financial forecasts.<br />\r\n- You&rsquo;ll also benefit from our strong industry connections, with opportunities for guest lectures, work experience, placements, and live projects.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- This is a top-up program for students who have already completed one of the following:<br />\r\n- Year two (Level 5) of a degree in Fashion, Textiles, or Business<br />\r\n- HND course in Fashion, Textiles, or Business<br />\r\n- Foundation degree in Fashion or Textiles</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you will need an overall IELTS score of 6.0, with at least 5.5 in each part, when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Management (Level 6 Top Up) | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Management (Level 6 Top Up) | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 09:29:48', '2024-09-14 09:29:48'),
(2094, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Fashion Management (Level 6 Top Up)', 'ba-hons-fashion-management-level-6-top-up', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Fashion Textile Design in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Fashion Textile Design at DMU teaches you the latest textile techniques and creative skills, preparing you for success in the fashion industry. In this course, you&#39;ll develop your artistic vision, learn new techniques, and shape your creative style for fashion-forward, luxury, and innovative designs. You&rsquo;ll create a portfolio that highlights your skills and design style, while also addressing social and environmental challenges in today&rsquo;s global fashion world.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>DMU accept applicants from different backgrounds:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n- Art and Design Foundation, or<br />\r\n- 112 points from at least 2 A-levels, or<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with DMM, or<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate with 26+ points, or<br />\r\n- T Levels with Merit<br />\r\nPlus, five GCSEs in grades 9-4, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or higher.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For Access courses, you need 30 Level 3 credits at Merit and GCSE English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or higher. Typically, students should have taken a break from full-time education before starting an Access course.<br />\r\nDMU also accept the BTEC First Diploma plus two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each part, when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Management (Level 6 Top Up) | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Fashion Management (Level 6 Top Up) | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 09:35:26', '2024-09-14 09:35:26'),
(2095, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Film Studies', 'ba-hons-film-studies', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Film Studies in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In today&#39;s media-driven world, this course helps turn your love for film and TV into a possible career, giving you the skills needed for many creative and technical jobs.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou&#39;ll learn about film history and theory, covering topics like Disney, Warner Bros, the business of film studios, world cinema, and fan cultures. You&rsquo;ll also build practical skills in filmmaking, film reviewing, working with screen archives, and planning film festivals.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThe course blends practical work with theory, helping you develop communication and critical thinking skills. Our graduates find jobs in film and TV, as well as other areas like finance, public relations, and tourism.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key features:</strong><br />\r\n- Study in a real cinema setting through our partnership with Leicester&rsquo;s Phoenix Cinema and Arts Centre, with opportunities for placements and to manage an annual film festival.<br />\r\n- Choose a specialisation in Creative Writing, Drama, English Literature, History, Journalism, or Media. These options will enhance your understanding of film and broaden your career possibilities.<br />\r\n- Learn from experts in our Cinema and Television History Research Institute, and attend guest lectures by well-known film directors, writers, and journalists.<br />\r\n- Graduates have worked for employers like the BBC and Odeon Entertainment in roles such as research, teaching, public relations, and film journalism.<br />\r\n- Gain international experience through the DMU Global programme, with trips to Hollywood, cinemas in Berlin, and the Cannes Film Festival.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Usually, you need 104 UCAS points from at least two A-levels or a BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with DMM grades. You also need five GCSEs at grade 4 or above, including English (or an equivalent qualification).</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Other qualifications we accept include:</strong><br />\r\n- A pass in a QAA-accredited Access to HE course with at least 30 level 3 credits at Merit, plus a separate English GCSE.<br />\r\n- We usually ask that students have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 24+ points.<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&#39;t your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with 5.5 in each section (or equivalent qualification) when you begin the course. English language classes are available through our British Council-accredited Centre for English Language Learning, both before and during the course if needed.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Film Studies | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Film Studies | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 09:38:49', '2024-09-14 09:38:49'),
(2096, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BSc (Hons) Finance and Investment', 'bsc-hons-finance-and-investment', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BSc (Hons) Finance and Investment in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Finance and Investment BSc course at DMU offers a solid academic foundation in finance, focusing on practical skills and career opportunities. You&#39;ll gain advanced technical knowledge and the right professional mindset needed to succeed in the finance industry. This course is part of the Chartered Financial Analysts (CFA) Affiliation Program, which helps prepare students for the CFA exams&mdash;one of the top qualifications in the finance world.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou&rsquo;ll learn about finance by exploring related subjects like accounting and economics. The course is great for students who enjoy working with numbers, as it focuses heavily on using data. You&rsquo;ll also work with industry-standard tools like Bloomberg, Thomson Reuters Eikon, Matlab, and Python to connect theory with real-world finance practices.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nNew and innovative modules, like Artificial Intelligence and Financial Applications, will give you hands-on experience in using and creating AI tools to solve real-world problems.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key features:</strong><br />\r\n- Gain advanced technical skills and professional attitudes for a successful career in finance and investment.<br />\r\n- Explore a wide range of topics, including finance, accounting, and economics.<br />\r\n- Learn about Artificial Intelligence in finance and gain experience in using and creating AI tools to solve real problems.<br />\r\n- The course is designed to meet many of the requirements of professional finance bodies and is a proud member of the CFA Affiliation Program.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You will usually need 104 UCAS points, which can come from at least two A-levels or a BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with DMM grades. You&rsquo;ll also need five GCSEs at grade 4 or higher, including English (or an equivalent qualification).</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Other accepted qualifications include:</strong><br />\r\n- A pass in an Access to HE course (approved by QAA) with at least 30 level 3 credits at Merit, plus a separate English GCSE.<br />\r\n- We usually ask that students have a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 24 points or more.<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or a similar test score) to start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'null', 'BSc (Hons) Finance and Investment | De Montfort University', 'BSc (Hons) Finance and Investment | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 10:25:47', '2024-09-14 10:25:47'),
(2097, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Fine Art', 'ba-hons-fine-art', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Fine Art in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this course, you&rsquo;ll have the freedom to explore many different art forms and develop your unique style. You can work with drawing, painting, sculpture, printmaking, video, photography, digital media, and installation art to create meaningful pieces that reflect today&rsquo;s complex world.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou&rsquo;ll spend about 70% of your time in the studio, improving your skills in making art, experimenting, and taking creative risks. Each year, you&rsquo;ll face new creative challenges and study art history, and contemporary practices, and work with local organizations. You&rsquo;ll also hear from visiting artists.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThe course is designed to meet the needs of today&rsquo;s global art scene and encourages you to explore themes like multiculturalism, identity, and art activism. You&rsquo;ll gain skills that will help you work as a fine artist or start a career in the creative industries.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- We&rsquo;ve been teaching art for over 120 years, and our course supports students in developing their creativity in a collaborative and experimental setting.<br />\r\n- The course includes practical topics like studio practice, curating exhibitions, marketing, and project planning.<br />\r\n- You&rsquo;ll study in our award-winning Vijay Patel Building, with access to Fine Art studios and 25 workshops equipped with industry-standard facilities.<br />\r\n- Students have showcased their work at events like the Handmade Festival, Two Queens Gallery, Attenborough Arts Centre, and other prestigious venues in the UK and internationally.<br />\r\n- Leicester is a vibrant city for creativity, with colourful street art, art festivals, and DMU&rsquo;s Leicester Gallery. Our city partnerships offer exciting opportunities to display your work, including at Leicester&rsquo;s LCB Depot.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Typical Entry Requirements</strong><br />\r\n- DMu accepts students from various backgrounds.<br />\r\n- Art and Design Foundation or<br />\r\n- 112 UCAS points from at least 2 A-levels<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with DMM grades<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26+ points or<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You also need five GCSEs at grades 9-4, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Alternative Qualifications:</strong><br />\r\n- Pass an Access to HE course with 30 Level 3 credits at Merit, plus a GCSE in English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or above. We usually ask that you take a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- BTEC First Diploma plus two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent qualification) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Fine Art | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Fine Art | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 10:32:23', '2024-09-14 10:32:23'),
(2098, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons)  Footwear Design', 'ba-hons-footwear-design', '£', '15750', '2000', 'With over 100 years of history, this course will give you the skills and experience needed to succeed in the footwear and fashion industry. In the Footwear Design degree, you will work closely with industry experts and well-known brands to learn about new products and technologies.\r\n\r\nDuring the course, you\'ll improve your shoe design and technical skills, focusing on how design and manufacturing work together to meet the needs of the footwear industry. You can choose to specialize in men’s, women’s, or children’s shoes, or even performance footwear, which is unique to this UK university.\r\n\r\nYou will develop skills in drawing, illustration, and prototyping, and learn how to present your ideas at a professional level. You\'ll also get hands-on experience making shoes using our modern studio equipment, including 3D design tools.\r\n\r\nEntry Requirements\r\n\r\nDMU welcome applicants from different backgrounds.\r\nYou can apply if you have:\r\nArt and Design Foundation or\r\n112 UCAS points from at least 2 A levels\r\nBTEC Extended Diploma with DMM grades\r\nInternational Baccalaureate with 26+ points or\r\nT Levels with Merit\r\nPlus, five GCSEs (grades 9-4), including English Language or Literature with at least a grade 4.\r\nIf you are applying through an Access Course, you need 30 Level 3 credits at Merit and a GCSE in English (Language or Literature) with a grade of 4 or above. Usually, DMU requires students to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.\r\nDMU also accept the BTEC First Diploma along with two GCSEs, including English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or higher.\r\n\r\nEnglish Language Requirements\r\n\r\nIf English is not your first language, you’ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall (with 5.5 in each band) or an equivalent score when you start the course.\r\n\r\nScholarships\r\n\r\nStudents admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of £1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to £2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of £2,500.\r\n\r\nMeta\r\n\r\nWant to study BA (Hons)  Footwear Design in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With over 100 years of history, this course will give you the skills and experience needed to succeed in the footwear and fashion industry. In the Footwear Design degree, you will work closely with industry experts and well-known brands to learn about new products and technologies.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">During the course, you&#39;ll improve your shoe design and technical skills, focusing on how design and manufacturing work together to meet the needs of the footwear industry. You can choose to specialize in men&rsquo;s, women&rsquo;s, or children&rsquo;s shoes, or even performance footwear, which is unique to this UK university.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You will develop skills in drawing, illustration, and prototyping, and learn how to present your ideas at a professional level. You&#39;ll also get hands-on experience making shoes using our modern studio equipment, including 3D design tools.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU welcome applicants from different backgrounds.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>You can apply if you have:</strong><br />\r\n- Art and Design Foundation or<br />\r\n- 112 UCAS points from at least 2 A levels<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with DMM grades<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate with 26+ points or<br />\r\n- T Levels with Merit<br />\r\n- Plus, five GCSEs (grades 9-4), including English Language or Literature with at least a grade 4.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If you are applying through an Access Course, you need 30 Level 3 credits at Merit and a GCSE in English (Language or Literature) with a grade of 4 or above. Usually, DMU requires students to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU also accept the BTEC First Diploma along with two GCSEs, including English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or higher.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall (with 5.5 in each band) or an equivalent score when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons)  Footwear Design | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons)  Footwear Design | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 10:37:23', '2024-09-14 10:37:23'),
(2099, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BSc (Hons) Forensic Science', 'bsc-hons-forensic-science', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BSc (Hons) Forensic Science in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Forensic science applies science to law by collecting, analyzing, interpreting, and presenting scientific evidence from crime scenes to the courtroom.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nIf you love solving scientific problems, enjoy using advanced equipment, and want to gain industry-specific knowledge and skills, this could be the perfect course for you. You can choose to study for a three-year BSc degree or a four-year integrated Master&#39;s (MSci).</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key features:</strong><br />\r\n- DMU&rsquo;s courses are developed with Leicestershire Police and accredited by The Chartered Society of Forensic Sciences, ensuring high-quality and up-to-date learning.<br />\r\n- You&#39;ll gain hands-on experience in our crime scene house, crime studio, crown court, and state-of-the-art forensic science labs.<br />\r\n- Strong industry links may offer you the chance to apply your skills in real-world settings through a year-long placement.<br />\r\n- DMU&rsquo;s teaching team includes experts and former professionals like Leisa Nichols-Drew, who has been recognized for her work on the forensic investigation of knife crime.<br />\r\n- Through DMU Global, students have gained unique international experiences, such as learning about human rights in Guatemala, attending court in New York, and helping refugees in Berlin.<br />\r\n- Graduates have gone on to work for top employers like the Home Office, National Crime Agency, GCHQ, AstraZeneca, and GlaxoSmithKline, among others.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>GCSEs: </strong>Five GCSEs at grade C/4 or higher, including Maths and English.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Plus one of the following:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- A-Level: At least 112 UCAS points (120 for MSci applicants) from two A levels, including a science subject (Biology, Chemistry, Physics, or Applied Sciences) with a grade of C or higher.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>BTEC:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- BTEC Extended Diploma in Science: DMM (DDM for MSci applicants).<br />\r\n- BTEC National Diploma in Science: DMM (DDM for MSci applicants).</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Alternative qualifications:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Access to HE Diploma: Pass a QAA Accredited Access to HE Diploma with 112 UCAS points (120 for MSci), including at least 15 Level 3 credits at distinction and 30 at merit. GCSE Maths and English at grade 4 or higher are required separately.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- International Baccalaureate: Score 26+ (28+ for MSci applicants) with 6 points in a science subject at a higher level.<br />\r\nEnglish Language Requirements</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- If English is not your first language, an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section, is required.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BSc (Hons) Forensic Science | De Montfort University', 'BSc (Hons) Forensic Science | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 10:41:06', '2024-09-14 10:41:06'),
(2100, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Game Art', 'ba-hons-game-art', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Game Art in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Combining creativity with specialist technology and strong industry connections, this degree will prepare you for roles like environment artist, character artist, lead artist, technical artist, or director.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This art degree, accredited by ScreenSkills, will help you master advanced 3D modelling skills while improving your 2D art abilities through courses like Game Production, Digital Art Practice, and Traditional Art Practice. You&rsquo;ll have the chance to create an industry-ready portfolio with help from your teachers and technical staff.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s top facilities include a dedicated games studio with industry-standard software, high-performance PCs and consoles for creating 3D game content, a drawing studio, Cintiq graphics tablets, and VR development equipment for students interested in virtual reality work.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Typical entry requirements:</strong><br />\r\n- DMU accept applicants from different backgrounds.<br />\r\n- 112 UCAS points from at least 2 A levels or similar qualifications, with Art and Design at grade B or above.<br />\r\n- Art and Design BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with a grade of DMM.<br />\r\n- Plus, five GCSEs at grade 4 or higher, including English or equivalent.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Other qualifications accepted:</strong><br />\r\n- Pass in a QAA accredited Access to HE Art and Design course with at least 15 level 3 credits in Art and Design at Distinction. English GCSE must be taken separately, as it cannot be counted within the Access course. We usually expect students to have taken a break from full-time education before doing the Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26+ points, including Art and Design at higher level grade 6.<br />\r\n- T Levels Merit.<br />\r\n- Art and Design Foundation Diploma: Pass.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each part (or equivalent) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Game Art | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Game Art | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 10:44:22', '2024-09-14 10:44:22'),
(2101, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BSc (Hons) Games Production', 'bsc-hons-games-production', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BSc (Hons) Games Production in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Video games have become bigger than the film, music, and video industries in the UK. DMU courses are designed to prepare you for jobs that need hands-on skills in gaming technologies.<br />\r\nYou&#39;ll get practical experience with popular game engines like Unity3D and Unreal Engine. You&#39;ll also learn sound engineering and how to create games for different platforms, such as consoles, mobile devices, and virtual/augmented reality. The course focuses on professionalism and has strong connections to BCS, The Chartered Institute for IT.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou&rsquo;ll study a variety of practical, technology-focused modules like Audio for Games, Advanced Game Engines, and Scripting and AI for Simulation. This will help you build a broad set of skills that you can use in the areas of game development that interest you. You&rsquo;ll also get to create a short game using the engine of your choice.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- Learn to use a range of game engines, 3D modelling software, and design tools so you can graduate ready for a career in game development. Graduates from our Computer Games Programming BSc now work at top gaming companies like Codemasters and Rockstar North.<br />\r\n- Study advanced topics like normal mapping and shader programming in Unity3D and Unreal, and learn how to export models from 3D tools like Maya, 3DS MAX, and Blender into your games.<br />\r\n- Access our game development studios, equipped with the latest technologies for creating and playing games on different platforms. These studios feature high-spec gaming computers and development software.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>To apply, you need:</strong><br />\r\n- 112 UCAS points from at least two A-levels, or<br />\r\n- A BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with grades DMM<br />\r\n- Plus, five GCSEs at grade 4 or above, including English and Mathematics or equivalent.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Other qualifications that we accept:</strong><br />\r\n- Pass in the QAA-accredited Access to HE course, with English and Mathematics GCSEs required separately. (We usually expect students to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.)<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26+ points<br />\r\n- T Levels Merit</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Langauge Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with at least 5.5 in each part (or equivalent) when you start the course. We also offer English language support through our British Council-accredited Centre for English Language Learning, both before and during the course if you need it.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BSc (Hons) Games Production | De Montfort University', 'BSc (Hons) Games Production | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 10:47:48', '2024-09-14 10:47:48');
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `country_id`, `university_id`, `campus_id`, `level_id`, `budget_id`, `name`, `slug`, `currency`, `fees`, `scholarship`, `description`, `overview`, `entry_requirements`, `scholarship_details`, `url`, `title`, `share_title`, `keywords`, `page_image`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(2102, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Global Arts Management (Level 6 Top Up)', 'ba-hons-global-arts-management-level-6-top-up', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Global Arts Management (Level 6 Top Up) in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This course will help you understand business management in the arts from an international point of view.<br />\r\nYou&rsquo;ll learn practical skills to become a leader in cultural fields like theatres, music venues, galleries, museums, and festivals. You&rsquo;ll study how politics and economics affect cultural products and services on different levels. As you progress, you can focus on areas that interest you most.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou&rsquo;ll also have the chance to be part of the Cultural eXchanges Festival, which has hosted famous guests like Benjamin Zephaniah, Meera Syal, and Dame Carol Ann Duffy.<br />\r\nThe course aims to prepare you for a career where you use management skills to promote artistic projects and balance the arts with business.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- Earn a degree in Global Arts Management in one year, then continue with a Cultural Events Management MSc.<br />\r\n- Develop skills in marketing, fundraising, business planning, licensing, health and safety, leadership, teamwork, programming, and cultural policy.<br />\r\n- Learn from experts in the field with strong connections to top organizations like Universal Music and London&rsquo;s Southbank Centre.<br />\r\n- Gain hands-on experience and networking opportunities by working on real projects and collaborating with arts organizations like Festival Republic, the Leicester Comedy Festival, and Curve Theatre.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Typical Entry Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>To join this program, you should have already completed:</strong><br />\r\n- The second year (Level 5) of a management or business-related degree, or<br />\r\n- An HND course in management or business, or<br />\r\n- If you&#39;re a mature student with different qualifications, we welcome your application if you have relevant experience.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent score) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Global Arts Management (Level 6 Top Up) | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Global Arts Management (Level 6 Top Up) | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 10:51:10', '2024-09-14 10:51:10'),
(2103, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Graphic Design', 'ba-hons-graphic-design', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Graphic Design in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Graphic design opens up many creative career options. You can work in advertising, animation, and visual effects, or even start your studio. With a graphic design degree, you can choose to work in an agency, as a freelancer, or in-house for a company.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nDuring your studies, you&#39;ll gain the experience needed to become a successful graphic designer and build a strong portfolio to show future employers. You&#39;ll not only learn to be creative but also develop skills in research, analysis, and entrepreneurship. Your teachers are experienced designers with industry connections, so you&#39;ll have the chance to work with real clients.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Here&#39;s what you typically need to get into the course:</strong><br />\r\n- A Levels: 104 UCAS points from at least two A-levels, with Art and Design at grade C or higher, or<br />\r\n- BTEC: Art and Design National Diploma/Extended Diploma with grades DMM<br />\r\n- GCSEs: Five GCSEs at grade 4 or higher, including English, or equivalent.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Alternative qualifications include:</strong><br />\r\n- Access Course: Pass the QAA-accredited Access to HE Art and Design course with at least 15 credits in Art and Design at merit. You must have English GCSE as a separate qualification. We usually prefer students to have had a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 24+ points, including Art and Design at higher level grade 5.<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit<br />\r\n- Art and Design Foundation Diploma: Pass.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&#39;t your first language, you&#39;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with at least 5.5 in each band (or equivalent) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Graphic Design | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Graphic Design | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-14 10:54:11', '2024-09-14 10:54:11'),
