(2185, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BSc (Hons) Health and Wellbeing in Society', 'bsc-hons-health-and-wellbeing-in-society', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BSc (Hons) Health and Wellbeing in Society in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This flexible degree program offers a dynamic way of learning, giving students a solid foundation to explore key public health issues in the UK today. Along with studying different theories, students learn how to apply them to current public health challenges. The program allows students to shape their studies to match their career interests, build confidence, and gain specialist skills that employers look for.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- The course is designed to help you get jobs in healthcare by developing skills that employers need.<br />\r\n- You can customize your learning to focus on areas that interest you, building both specialized knowledge and general skills useful for many career paths.<br />\r\n- Enjoy a supportive learning environment with a personal tutor to guide you throughout your studies.<br />\r\n- You&rsquo;ll explore topics like the psychology and sociology of health, debates in healthcare, and mental health and wellbeing.<br />\r\n- The &quot;Health, Wellbeing and Society in Professional Contexts&quot; module gives you the chance to gain work experience in different health and community settings.<br />\r\n- Graduates often pursue careers in health promotion, working with community groups, charities, and local governments. Many also go on to further study, like a Master by Research at DMU.<br />\r\n- Throughout the course, you&rsquo;ll examine a wide range of health-related issues, especially focusing on wellbeing. Topics covered include health psychology, public health, health promotion, social care management, and health inequalities. In your third year, you can choose optional modules such as Substance Use, Addictive Behavior and Health, Mental Health and Wellbeing, and Social Exclusion and Health.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>GCSEs:</strong><br />\r\n- Five GCSEs at grade C/4 or above, including English and Maths.<br />\r\n<strong>Plus one of the following:</strong><br />\r\nA Levels:<br />\r\n- At least 104 UCAS points from 2 or more A levels.<br />\r\nT Levels:<br />\r\n- Merit.<br />\r\nBTEC:<br />\r\n- BTEC National Diploma with Distinction/Merit/Merit.<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with Distinction/Merit/Merit.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For more details about BTEC equivalents, check the relevant information.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Access Course:</strong><br />\r\n- Pass the QAA Access to HE course with 104 UCAS points and 30 Level 3 credits at Merit.<br />\r\n- Normally, students need to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate:<br />\r\n- 24+ points.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirement</strong>s</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you&#39;ll need an IELTS score of 6.5 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent score) when starting the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'null', 'BSc (Hons) Health and Wellbeing in Society | University of Hertfordshire', 'BSc (Hons) Health and Wellbeing in Society | University of Hertfordshire', NULL, NULL, 1, 13, 13, '2024-09-17 06:22:13', '2024-09-17 06:28:43'),
(2186, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) History', 'ba-hons-history', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) History in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s course focuses on modern and contemporary history and covers a wide range of topics from around the world. You&rsquo;ll learn about European and non-European histories, including subjects like colonialism, decolonisation, immigration, ethnic minorities, and gender.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThis course will help you develop strong skills in absorbing, communicating, and critically analyzing complex information. As you move forward in your studies, you&rsquo;ll explore deeper topics and focus on your historical interests. A team of passionate experts will guide you through a variety of teaching and assessment methods.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou&rsquo;ll study the histories of Britain, South Asia, Europe, Africa, and the Americas, along with unique topics such as the history of photography and the history of sport and leisure. You can also choose to study English Literature or Education alongside your history degree.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key features:</strong><br />\r\n- Gain valuable skills in researching and communicating complex information, helping you build careers in teaching, law, marketing, and museums.<br />\r\n&nbsp;- Specialize in areas like photographic history, the history of sport and leisure, war and conflict, migration, ethnicity, and racism.<br />\r\n- Choose to study additional subjects like English Literature or Education to broaden your skills and career options after graduation.<br />\r\n- Learn from internationally recognized academics who use innovative teaching methods and invite guest speakers to enhance your learning experience.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Typical entry requirements:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- 112 points from at least 2 A-levels, or<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with grades DMM, or<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26+ points, or<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Additionally, you need five GCSEs with grades 9-4, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or higher.<br />\r\nIf you&#39;re applying through an Access course, you need 30 level 3 credits at Merit and a GCSE in English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or above. Typically, students are expected to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\nWe also accept a BTEC First Diploma along with two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or higher.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&#39;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent score) when you begin the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) History | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) History | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 13, NULL, '2024-09-17 06:36:19', '2024-09-17 06:36:19');
