(2187, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) History with Mandarin', 'ba-hons-history-with-mandarin', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) History with Mandarin in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s History program is broad, globally focused, and innovative. It mainly looks at modern and contemporary history and teaches you valuable research and analytical skills, helping you learn how to understand, communicate, and think critically about complex information.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThe course reflects the global world we live in and covers British, South Asian, European, African, and North and South American history. It explores important topics like colonialism, decolonization, immigration, ethnic minorities, gender, photography, and the history of sports and leisure.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nAs you progress, you&rsquo;ll dive deeper into topics that interest you, while being guided by passionate teachers who are experts in their fields. They will create a lively learning environment with various teaching and assessment methods.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nIn addition to history, you will also study Mandarin at either beginner or post-beginner levels, developing your language skills and understanding of China&rsquo;s culture, politics, history, and art.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">-Focus on unique areas like photography, the history of sport and leisure, war, migration, ethnicity, and racism.<br />\r\n- Build valuable skills like researching and communicating complex information. These skills can lead to careers in teaching, law, marketing, or working in museums and heritage sites.<br />\r\n- Learn Mandarin at a pace that suits you, while also gaining knowledge about Chinese society and culture.<br />\r\n- Be taught by top experts and attend lectures from guest speakers.<br />\r\n- Enjoy organized visits to archives and museums like the National Archives in London and access historical collections at DMU, including the Stephen Lawrence Papers, the Ski Club of GB archive, and the Kodak collection.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- 112 points from at least 2 A levels or<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with DMM or<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate with 26+ points or<br />\r\n- T Levels with Merit</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Plus, five GCSEs (grades 9-4) including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If you&#39;re taking an Access course, you need to pass with 30 Level 3 credits at Merit and have GCSE English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or above.<br />\r\nStudents who take the Access course usually need to have had a break from full-time education.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We also accept the BTEC First Diploma plus two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.<br />\r\n- No interview is required.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you will need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with at least 5.5 in each band (or an equivalent test) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) History with Mandarin | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) History with Mandarin | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 13, NULL, '2024-09-17 06:43:05', '2024-09-17 06:43:05'),
(2188, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) History Politics and International Relations', 'ba-hons-history-politics-and-international-relations', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) History Politics and International Relations in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s program is broad, globally focused, and innovative. You&#39;ll learn important research and analysis skills, which will help you take in, communicate, and carefully examine complex information.<br />\r\nIn line with our global world, the History curriculum covers a variety of modern and contemporary European and non-European histories. It explores key topics like colonialism, decolonisation, immigration, ethnic minorities, racism, and gender.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou will also learn about politics on local, national, and global levels. You&rsquo;ll dive into important issues in today&rsquo;s international politics, and our curriculum gives you both practical tools and theoretical knowledge to understand political issues and handle current social, political, and economic challenges.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nKey features:</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Explore unique areas like the history of photography, sport and leisure, war and conflict, migration, ethnicity, and racism.<br />\r\n- Specialise in History, Politics, or International Relations as you move through your studies.<br />\r\n- Develop strong skills in researching and communicating complex information. These skills are useful in careers like teaching, law, marketing, and the heritage and museum sector.<br />\r\n- Learn from renowned academics and gain extra insight through trips to archives and museums like The National Archives in London.<br />\r\n- DMU is the only UK university to host both &lsquo;Congress to Campus&rsquo; and &lsquo;European Parliament to Campus&rsquo; events, where you&rsquo;ll hear from important political figures.<br />\r\n- Apply your skills in real-world placements. Past students have gained experience at places like a regional newspaper, the King Richard III Visitor Centre, the House of Commons, and local governments.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>To apply for the course:</strong><br />\r\n- You need 112 points from at least 2 A levels, or<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with DMM, or<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate with 26+ points, or<br />\r\n- T Levels with Merit.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You also need five GCSEs at grades 9-4, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or higher.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For Access courses, you need 30 level 3 credits at Merit and GCSE English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or above.<br />\r\nStudents usually need to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\nWe also accept the BTEC First Diploma along with two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with 5.5 in each part (or equivalent) before starting the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) History Politics and International Relations | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) History Politics and International Relations | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 13, NULL, '2024-09-17 06:48:25', '2024-09-17 06:48:25'),
(2189, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Human Resource Management', 'ba-hons-human-resource-management', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Human Resource Management in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Studying Human Resource Management at DMU helps you understand important topics in modern management, work, and employment. The degree follows the key ideas, values, and skills of the Chartered Institute of Personnel Development (CIPD).</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThe course offers a wide range of career options. You will learn about managing employee relationships, promoting equality and diversity, helping with learning and development, improving organisations, and tackling key issues in HR. To help you get ready for your career, you will also develop important skills that employers look for, such as business knowledge, self-awareness, emotional intelligence, project management, and an understanding of how people and organisations behave.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features</strong><br />\r\n- DMU is one of the few respected CIPD Approved Centres. CIPD is the leading HR professional body in the UK and internationally, known by employers as a mark of quality in HR practice.<br />\r\n- DMU&rsquo;s courses are designed to boost your job prospects. Graduates have gone on to work for well-known companies like Telegraph Media Group, Jaguar Land Rover, PwC, and Mondelez.<br />\r\n- Many of our teachers have years of real-world experience and bring practical techniques into the classroom.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>GCSEs</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">-You need five GCSEs with grades 4 or above, including English and Maths.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Plus, one of the following:</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A levels<br />\r\n- You will need at least two A levels or similar qualifications like BTECs, with a total of 112 UCAS points.<br />\r\nT Levels<br />\r\n- Merit<br />\r\nBTEC<br />\r\n- BTEC National Diploma: Distinction/Distinction/Merit<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma: Distinction/Distinction/Merit</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Other qualifications:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- A pass in the QAA-accredited Access to HE course with 112 UCAS points, including 30 Level 3 credits at Merit.<br />\r\n- You must also have separate GCSEs in English and Maths (equivalents in the Access course are not accepted).<br />\r\n- Students taking the Access course usually need to have had a break from full-time education.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26+ points.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, an IELTS score of 6.0 overall (with at least 5.5 in each part) or equivalent is typically required.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Human Resource Management | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Human Resource Management | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 13, NULL, '2024-09-17 06:58:21', '2024-09-17 06:58:21'),
