(2803, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Illustration with Graphic Design', 'ba-hons-illustration-with-graphic-design', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Illustration with Graphic Design in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Illustration with Graphic Design course helps you build your skills in creating images, designs, and illustrations. You&#39;ll work on various projects across digital, motion, and print platforms to express your unique style.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nIn this course, you&#39;ll learn how to understand project requirements, solve problems, and come up with creative design solutions. You&#39;ll work on real industry projects and competition briefs, which will help you understand the field better.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThe course supports your career as an illustrator and creative professional. In your first year, you&#39;ll focus on basic drawing and design skills. In the second year, you&#39;ll start developing your style through creative projects and workshops. By the third year, you&#39;ll prepare for the professional world with hands-on experiences and guidance to help you enter the creative industry.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>To join the Illustration with Graphic Design course, you usually need:</strong><br />\r\n- 104 UCAS points from at least two A-levels or similar qualifications, with a grade of C or above in Art and Design, or<br />\r\n- A BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma in Art and Design with grades DMM, and<br />\r\n- Five GCSEs at grade C or above, including English or an equivalent subject.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Other qualifications that are accepted include:</strong><br />\r\n- A pass in the QAA-accredited Access to HE Art and Design course with at least 15 credits in Art and Design at merit. You also need a separate GCSE in English, as it can&#39;t be included in the Access course. We typically ask for a break from full-time education before starting the Access course, or<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 24+ points, with Art and Design at a higher level grade 5, or<br />\r\n- T Levels with a Merit, or<br />\r\n- Art and Design Foundation Diploma with a Pass.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you will need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent score) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Illustration with Graphic Design | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Illustration with Graphic Design | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, 15, '2024-09-20 11:11:23', '2024-09-20 11:13:41'),
(2804, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Interior Design', 'ba-hons-interior-design', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Interior Design in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this course, you&#39;ll reimagine existing spaces and create new, innovative environments. You&#39;ll learn how to design interiors that focus on how people interact with their surroundings, making sure the spaces are comfortable, practical, effective, beautiful, and emotionally engaging.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou&#39;ll work on transforming real buildings and sites into exciting new spaces for different uses, like exhibitions, retail, leisure, performances, dining, and socializing. You&#39;ll also build skills in drawing, 3D modeling, computer-aided design (CAD), virtual reality, and video modeling. Your work will address future global challenges and emphasize sustainability and inclusivity.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou&rsquo;ll develop your own design style and learn how to confidently present your creative ideas. The goal is to help you graduate as a skilled designer with a strong portfolio ready for the industry.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key features:</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Work in a studio that simulates real-world practice and learn from experienced professionals.<br />\r\n- Choose your own design projects based on what interests you. Previous students have created everything from immersive art galleries to boutique hotels and have tackled issues like food waste and empty shops.<br />\r\n- Improve your job prospects with a placement. Students have gained experience with companies like Ashfield Events, Newman Gauge, Tibbatts Abel, and PVH Europe.<br />\r\n- Build your portfolio by entering competitions and showcasing your work. Students have been recognized in national awards and exhibited their projects at events like New Designers in London.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Typical entry requirements</strong><br />\r\nWe welcome students from different backgrounds. To apply, you usually need:<br />\r\n- An Art and Design Foundation course, or<br />\r\n- 112 UCAS points from at least 2 A levels, or<br />\r\n- A BTEC Extended Diploma with DMM grades, or<br />\r\n- An International Baccalaureate with 26+ points, or<br />\r\n- T Levels with a Merit grade</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Plus, five GCSEs in grades 9-4, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or higher.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Alternatively, you can:</strong><br />\r\nPass an Access course with 30 Level 3 credits at Merit and GCSE English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or higher. (We usually prefer students to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.)<br />\r\nHave a BTEC First Diploma plus two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or higher.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you&#39;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each part, or an equivalent score when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Interior Design | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Interior Design | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-20 11:17:23', '2024-09-20 11:17:23'),
(2805, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) International Business', 'ba-hons-international-business', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) International Business in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In our world today, everything is more connected than ever before. As global economies grow closer, businesses and individuals face new challenges and opportunities. Many companies want to explore international markets and engage in global business activities, creating a high demand for people who understand how international business works.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThe International Business BA (Hons) degree is designed to give you the latest knowledge about key issues in international business. This course will help you gain the skills needed to succeed in a global market, whether you&#39;re expanding a business abroad or trading internationally. You&#39;ll learn how businesses operate locally and across borders.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- Global Career Opportunities: This degree can open doors to careers around the world.<br />\r\n- Comprehensive Modules: You&#39;ll study how multinational companies work, explore business in emerging markets, understand economic geography, and learn about trade management.<br />\r\n- Focus on Employability: The course includes guest lectures, field trips, real-life case studies, and assignments related to business needs.<br />\r\n- Career Support: Our Careers Team helps you build the skills and experience employers look for, with opportunities for placements at companies like Rolls Royce, IBM, Walt Disney, the NHS, and Siemens.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">GCSEs:<br />\r\n- Five GCSEs at grade 4 or higher, including English and Maths.<br />\r\nPlus one of the following:<br />\r\n- A Levels:<br />\r\nYou need 112 UCAS points from at least two A Levels or equivalent (like BTEC).<br />\r\n- T Levels:<br />\r\nMerit.<br />\r\n- BTEC:<br />\r\n- BTEC National Diploma: Distinction/Distinction/Merit.<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma: Distinction/Distinction/Merit.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Alternative Qualifications:</strong><br />\r\n- Pass a QAA-accredited Access to HE course with a total of 112 UCAS points, including at least 30 Level 3 credits at Merit. You must have separate GCSEs in English and Maths (equivalents are not accepted). Usually, we prefer that you take a break from full-time education before doing the Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26 or more points.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong><br />\r\nIf English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent test score).</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) International Business | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) International Business | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-20 11:21:14', '2024-09-20 11:21:14'),
(2806, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) International Finance and Business', 'ba-hons-international-finance-and-business', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) International Finance and Business in the UK? Let’s check the scholarship entry requirements and features of this course', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This practical, career-focused course is perfect for those interested in how businesses compete and work together around the world. It&rsquo;s designed to build on what you learned in your higher education degrees or diplomas and prepare you for an international career or a Master&rsquo;s program.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>What You&#39;ll Learn:</strong><br />\r\nBusiness Modules: Understand broad business concepts, models, and issues with a focus on leadership and innovation.<br />\r\nFinance Modules: Improve your skills in analyzing and solving problems related to risk management, banking systems, and financial markets.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- Global Perspective: Learn about businesses and their activities around the world.<br />\r\n- International Experience: Take part in DMU Global&#39;s work and study opportunities abroad to broaden your cultural experiences.<br />\r\n- Up-to-Date Knowledge: Benefit from lecturers who have real-world experience and work with major organizations.<br />\r\n- Innovative Assessments: Develop skills that employers value, such as creativity, organization, and communication.<br />\r\n- Trading Floor: Gain hands-on experience with real-life trading environments on campus and online. Access industry-standard financial and economic data, and use self-study certifications and training materials from LSEG Workspace and Bloomberg.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This is a top-up program, which means it&#39;s designed to build on your existing qualifications. We accept applications from students with different types of qualifications and recognize international qualifications equivalent to an HND.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&#39;t your first language, you&#39;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 or an equivalent level of English.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) International Finance and Business | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) International Finance and Business | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-20 11:23:49', '2024-09-20 11:23:49'),
(2807, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) International Tourism and Hospitality Management (Level 6 Top Up)', 'ba-hons-international-tourism-and-hospitality-management-level-6-top-up', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) International Tourism and Hospitality Management (Level 6 Top Up) in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and features', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Tourism and Hospitality are big, growing fields around the world. This top-up degree will give you the latest industry knowledge and help you build useful skills for management roles in these fields.<br />\r\nYou&rsquo;ll learn about tourism and hospitality, focusing on marketing, branding, sustainability, and leadership. You&rsquo;ll also practice solving industry problems and making smart decisions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThis course will prepare you for a career in tourism and hospitality, helping you understand different cultures and consumer behaviors. You&rsquo;ll even have the chance to visit a European city for real-world research.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- Earn your degree in International Tourism and Hospitality Management in just one year, and you can continue on to a Cultural Events Management MSc.<br />\r\n- Work with travel agents, tour operators, airports, major brands, and independent hotels.<br />\r\n- Take part in exciting events and trips with local and European tourism and hospitality providers.<br />\r\n- Study modern topics like natural and cultural tourism, eco-tourism, and their impact on the industry.<br />\r\n- Learn from industry experts who are involved in current research and know the latest trends and challenges.<br />\r\n- Enjoy block teaching, where you focus on one subject at a time, receive regular feedback, and balance your studies and life well.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Typical Entry Requirements</strong><br />\r\n- This top-up program is for students who have already completed:<br />\r\n- The second year (Level 5) of a management or business degree, or<br />\r\n- An HND in management or business.<br />\r\n- We also welcome applications from mature students with non-standard qualifications, as long as they have relevant experience to go with their qualifications.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or an equivalent score) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) International Tourism and Hospitality Management (Level 6 Top Up) | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) International Tourism and Hospitality Management (Level 6 Top Up) | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-20 11:26:28', '2024-09-20 11:26:28');
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `country_id`, `university_id`, `campus_id`, `level_id`, `budget_id`, `name`, `slug`, `currency`, `fees`, `scholarship`, `description`, `overview`, `entry_requirements`, `scholarship_details`, `url`, `title`, `share_title`, `keywords`, `page_image`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(2808, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) International Tourism and Hospitality Management', 'ba-hons-international-tourism-and-hospitality-management', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) International Tourism and Hospitality Management in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and features', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Tourism and Hospitality is one of the fastest-growing industries in the world. This course will help you learn important skills for managing tourism and hospitality internationally, improving your chances of building a successful career in this expanding industry.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou&#39;ll explore both the theory and practice of tourism and hospitality, with a focus on sustainability, innovation, resilience, and leadership. You&#39;ll also learn how to solve complex industry problems and make smart decisions using critical thinking.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThis course will prepare you for an exciting global career by helping you understand different cultures, consumer behaviour, and how to use digital tools for decision-making. You&#39;ll also gain real-world experience through placements and a research project.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nThe course is closely connected to Arts and Festivals Management at DMU, which was ranked number one in the UK for &lsquo;Hospitality, Event Management and Tourism&rsquo; by the Guardian University Guide 2023.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Key features:</strong><br />\r\n- You&#39;ll work with travel agents, tour operators, airports, major tourism brands, and independent hotels.<br />\r\n- You&#39;ll take part in exciting events with local, national, and European tourism and hospitality providers, including a DMU Global trip.<br />\r\n- You&#39;ll study topics essential for your career, such as sustainable travel, digital marketing in the industry, and a research trip to a European city.<br />\r\n- You&#39;ll learn from top industry experts who are involved in international research, giving you the latest insights on industry practices and challenges.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Typical entry requirements:</strong><br />\r\n- 112 points from at least 2 A-levels, or<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma with DMM, or<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26+ points, or<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You also need five GCSEs with grades 9-4, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or higher.<br />\r\nIf you&#39;re applying with an Access course, you&#39;ll need 30 Level 3 credits at Merit (or equivalent) and GCSE English (Language or Literature) at grade 4 or above. Typically, students will need to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\nWe also accept the BTEC First Diploma plus two GCSEs, including English Language or Literature at grade 4 or above.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&#39;t your first language, you&#39;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with 5.5 in each section (or equivalent) before starting the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) International Tourism and Hospitality Management | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) International Tourism and Hospitality Management | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 05:34:31', '2024-09-21 05:34:31'),
(2809, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Journalism', 'ba-hons-journalism', '£', '15250', '2000', 'Journalists play an important role in a democracy, and this course offers the chance to build an exciting career that helps inform public debate on important issues that affect our lives.\r\nThe course is flexible, allowing you to focus on areas that interest you, like music journalism, lifestyle, or sports, while also encouraging you to challenge the status quo. Throughout the degree, you\'ll explore topics like social equality, justice, protest, and marginalized communities in the UK.\r\nYou will learn essential skills like researching, interviewing, writing, and publishing online, along with multimedia skills in video and audio production. The journalism industry looks for graduates with strong digital skills, knowledge of media law, political systems, and the ability to question societal structures.\r\nKey features:\r\nBuild practical skills in the Leicester Centre for Journalism and our Creative Technology Studios, which include radio production studios and film studios with high-tech equipment like multi-cameras and green screens.\r\nLearn from experienced journalists and academic experts who work in newspapers, radio, magazines, and digital journalism. For example, students recently heard from successful freelance writer and former DMU Journalism student, Rachel Toal.\r\nYou can choose to specialize in Creative Writing, Drama, English Literature, Film Studies, History, or Media, which will enhance your understanding and open up more career options.\r\nGet hands-on experience by joining student societies like the award-winning Demon Media group, where you can contribute to its magazine, radio, YouTube channel, and website.\r\nGain work experience with placements in companies like The Times, Sky Sports, NME, Leicester City Football Club, ITN, the BBC, CNN, Leicestershire Live, and the Observer.\r\nGraduates have gone on to work or intern at top UK media companies, including Sky News, The Sun, the BBC, CNN, ITV, Mixmag, and Clash magazines, as well as PR companies and digital media firms.\r\n\r\nEntry Requirements\r\nA typical offer is usually 104 UCAS points from at least two A-levels or a BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with DMM. You\'ll also need five GCSEs at grade 4 or higher, including English or an equivalent qualification.\r\nOther qualifications include:\r\nA Pass in the QAA-accredited Access to HE course. English and Maths GCSEs are still required separately as the Access course doesn’t count for these subjects. Students are usually expected to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.\r\nInternational Baccalaureate: 24+ points.\r\nT Levels: Merit.\r\n\r\nEnglish Language Requirements\r\n\r\nIf English isn\'t your first language, you\'ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each part (or equivalent).\r\nScholarships\r\n\r\nStudents admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of £1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to £2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of £2,500.\r\n\r\nMeta\r\n\r\nWant to study BA (Hons) Journalism in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and key features of this course at DMU', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Journalists play an important role in a democracy, and this course offers the chance to build an exciting career that helps inform public debate on important issues that affect our lives.<br />\r\nThe course is flexible, allowing you to focus on areas that interest you, like music journalism, lifestyle, or sports, while also encouraging you to challenge the status quo. Throughout the degree, you&#39;ll explore topics like social equality, justice, protest, and marginalized communities in the UK.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou will learn essential skills like researching, interviewing, writing, and publishing online, along with multimedia skills in video and audio production. The journalism industry looks for graduates with strong digital skills, knowledge of media law, political systems, and the ability to question societal structures.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key features:</strong><br />\r\n- Build practical skills in the Leicester Centre for Journalism and our Creative Technology Studios, which include radio production studios and film studios with high-tech equipment like multi-cameras and green screens.<br />\r\n- Learn from experienced journalists and academic experts who work in newspapers, radio, magazines, and digital journalism. For example, students recently heard from successful freelance writer and former DMU Journalism student, Rachel Toal.<br />\r\n- You can choose to specialize in Creative Writing, Drama, English Literature, Film Studies, History, or Media, which will enhance your understanding and open up more career options.<br />\r\n- Get hands-on experience by joining student societies like the award-winning Demon Media group, where you can contribute to its magazine, radio, YouTube channel, and website.<br />\r\n- Gain work experience with placements in companies like The Times, Sky Sports, NME, Leicester City Football Club, ITN, the BBC, CNN, Leicestershire Live, and the Observer.<br />\r\n- Graduates have gone on to work or intern at top UK media companies, including Sky News, The Sun, the BBC, CNN, ITV, Mixmag, and Clash magazines, as well as PR companies and digital media firms.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A typical offer is usually 104 UCAS points from at least two A-levels or a BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with DMM. You&#39;ll also need five GCSEs at grade 4 or higher, including English or an equivalent qualification.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Other qualifications include:</strong><br />\r\n- A Pass in the QAA-accredited Access to HE course. English and Maths GCSEs are still required separately as the Access course doesn&rsquo;t count for these subjects. Students are usually expected to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 24+ points.<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&#39;t your first language, you&#39;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each part (or equivalent).</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Journalism | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Journalism | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 05:37:48', '2024-09-21 05:37:48'),
(2810, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'Law LLB (Hons)', 'law-llb-hons', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study Law LLB (Hons) in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and key features of this course at DMU', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s Law LLB program, created by legal experts, gives you a strong foundation in law while allowing you to focus on the area of law that interests you the most, with six pathways to choose from</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The course is hands-on, and you&rsquo;ll enhance your learning with activities designed to boost your employability. You&rsquo;ll practice in our dedicated law spaces, including a mock courtroom and a client interview room, helping you gain practical skills for the workplace.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Whether you aim to continue studying or start your career, you&#39;ll be well-prepared through various learning methods, such as presentations, essays, and problem-solving tasks.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>GCSE Requirements:</strong><br />\r\n- You need five GCSEs at grade 4 or higher, including English and Maths.<br />\r\n<strong>Plus one of the following:</strong><br />\r\n- A Levels<br />\r\nA typical offer is 120 UCAS points. You must study at least two A-level subjects or an equivalent qualification like BTEC.<br />\r\n- T Levels<br />\r\n- Merit</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>BTEC</strong><br />\r\n- BTEC National Diploma: Distinction/Distinction/Merit<br />\r\n-BTEC Extended Diploma: Distinction/Distinction/Merit</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Other qualifications</strong><br />\r\n- Pass the QAA-accredited Access to HE course with 120 UCAS points, including at least 30 Level 3 credits at Merit.<br />\r\n- English and Maths GCSEs are required separately, as the Access course doesn&rsquo;t count for these.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&#39;t your first language, you&#39;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or equivalent), before starting the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'Law LLB (Hons) | De Montfort University', 'Law LLB (Hons) | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 05:41:35', '2024-09-21 05:41:35'),
(2811, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Marketing', 'ba-hons-marketing', '£', '15750', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Marketing in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and key features of this course at DMU', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s Marketing BA course gives you a deep understanding of modern marketing and how it fits into business and society.<br />\r\nYou&rsquo;ll learn how to choose and use the right methods to solve marketing challenges faced by major companies around the world. You&rsquo;ll also explore new trends and gain real-world experience through partnerships with top digital marketing agencies, helping you develop the skills needed for a career in marketing.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou&rsquo;ll get to know different areas of marketing, how they connect, and how to apply them in practice. For example, you&rsquo;ll learn about customers, markets, brands, and market research, and use this knowledge to create effective marketing solutions. This will help you build the skills to make a positive impact in the world.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key features:</strong><br />\r\n- The course structure creates a supportive learning environment, allowing you to master marketing principles step by step, no matter your learning style or background.<br />\r\n- Special modules will help you prepare for the fast-paced, creative marketing industry.<br />\r\n- We focus on career preparation with practical modules like Integrated Marketing Communications. For example, students worked on a real project for Samsung, applying theory to real-life marketing.<br />\r\n- The course is recognized by respected professional bodies like the Chartered Institute of Marketing and the Institute of Data and Marketing.<br />\r\n- DMU&rsquo;s innovative assessments help build your digital and marketing skills by working through real-world scenarios, preparing you for a graduate career.<br />\r\n- You can participate in large projects like X-Culture, where one of our students, Emily Le Ngoc, was the only British winner of the global business competition.<br />\r\n- Learn about new trends in marketing, including sustainability marketing, digital transformation, creativity, and engaging more diverse consumers.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">GCSEs:<br />\r\nYou need five GCSEs at grade 4 or higher, including English and Maths.<br />\r\nA Levels:<br />\r\n-A typical offer is 112 UCAS points. You need to study at least two subjects at A Level or equivalent (like BTEC).<br />\r\nT Levels:<br />\r\nYou need a Merit grade.<br />\r\nBTEC:<br />\r\n- BTEC National Diploma: Distinction/Distinction/Merit<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma: Distinction/Distinction/Merit</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Alternative Qualifications:<br />\r\n- Pass in the QAA-accredited Access to HE course with 112 UCAS points overall and at least 30 Level 3 credits at Merit. You also need separate GCSEs in English and Maths; they can&rsquo;t be combined within the Access course. Usually, you should have had a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26 points or more.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language an IELTS score of 6.0 overall with 5.5 in each band (or equivalent) when you start the course is essential. English language tuition, delivered by our British Council-accredited Centre for English Language Learning.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Marketing | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Marketing | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 05:46:12', '2024-09-21 05:46:12'),
(2812, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BSc (Hons) Mathematics', 'bsc-hons-mathematics', '£', '16250', '2000', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'null', 'BSc (Hons) Mathematics | De Montfort University', 'BSc (Hons) Mathematics | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 05:50:33', '2024-09-21 05:50:33'),
(2813, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BEng (Hons)  Mechanical Engineering', 'beng-hons-mechanical-engineering', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BEng (Hons)  Mechanical Engineering in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and key features of this course at DMU', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s course is based on the latest research in areas like aerodynamics, fluid systems, transportation, manufacturing, and sustainable development. We use our Mechanical Engineering Laboratory to study things like thermofluids, solid mechanics, and dynamics.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You will gain essential problem-solving skills by taking courses on General Engineering Tools, Principles, and Mechanical Design and Manufacturing. You&rsquo;ll also develop professional skills through modules like Design and Project Management, Advanced Mechanical Materials, and Engineering Business Environment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You can choose to study Mechanical Engineering in two ways: as a three-year BEng (Hons) program or a four-year integrated master&rsquo;s program. After three years, you can either graduate with a BEng degree or continue for an extra year to earn an MEng, if you meet the requirements.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To get a typical offer for the BEng or MEng in Mechanical Engineering, you need:<br />\r\n- 112 UCAS points from at least two A-levels, including Mathematics or Physics at grade C or above, or<br />\r\n- Engineering or Physics BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with DMM (DDM for MEng), or<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate with 26+ points and Maths or Physics at higher level, or<br />\r\n- T Levels with a Merit grade, or<br />\r\n- Engineering Year Zero: Pass<br />\r\nYou also need five GCSEs at grade 4 or above, including English and Mathematics or equivalent.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you&rsquo;ll need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each section (or equivalent) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BEng (Hons)  Mechanical Engineering | De Montfort University', 'BEng (Hons)  Mechanical Engineering | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 05:53:42', '2024-09-21 05:53:42'),
(2814, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BEng (Hons)  Mechatronics and Robotics', 'beng-hons-mechatronics-and-robotics', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BEng (Hons)  Mechatronics and Robotics in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and key features of this course at DMU', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Mechatronics and Robotics BEng/MEng program focuses on combining mechanical, electronic, and control systems to create complete products, machines, or processes. This field uses special design methods and tools to make systems that are simpler, cheaper, and more reliable. Mechatronics and Robotics engineers are in high demand because of their wide-ranging skills.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>What You&#39;ll Study:</strong><br />\r\n- The course balances important technical subjects with professional skills, preparing you to handle tough engineering problems.<br />\r\n- You&#39;ll develop management skills throughout the course to work effectively as a multidisciplinary engineer.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Course Options:</strong><br />\r\n- You can choose a three-year BEng (Hons) program or a four-year integrated master&rsquo;s program. After three years, you can either graduate with a BEng or continue for another year to earn an MEng, if you meet the requirements.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- Accreditation: The course is accredited by the Institution of Mechanical Engineers (IMechE) and the Institute of Engineering and Technology (IET), which helps you work towards becoming a Chartered Engineer.<br />\r\n- Experienced Staff: Learn from knowledgeable teachers who will help you understand engineering principles and develop professional skills.<br />\r\n- Facilities: Study in well-equipped labs, including a large mechanical engineering lab, specialized labs for materials, dynamics, and control, and an Engine Test Cell.<br />\r\n- Work Placement: Gain practical experience with a 12-month work placement. Students have worked with big companies like Rolls Royce and the DMU Racing team.<br />\r\n- Student Societies: Join student groups like DMU Flyers, Electronics Club, and DMU Racing to connect with other engineering students and get hands-on experience.<br />\r\n- International Experience: Enhance your studies with DMU Global opportunities, such as exploring skyscraper engineering in New York or visiting the BMW Motorrad factory in Berlin.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Five GCSEs at grade 4 or above, including English and Mathematics (or equivalent).<br />\r\nPlus one of the following:<br />\r\n- Normally 112 UCAS points (120 for MEng) from at least two A-levels or equivalent, including Mathematics or Physics at grade 4 or above.<br />\r\n- Engineering or Physics BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with DMM (DDM for MEng).</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Other accepted qualifications:<br />\r\n- Pass in one of these QAA accredited Access to HE courses:<br />\r\n- Access to HE Engineering<br />\r\n- Engineering Science<br />\r\n- Engineering Science and Mathematics<br />\r\n- Physics and Engineering<br />\r\n- Physics and Mathematics<br />\r\n- Electronics and Computer Engineering</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- If you are studying a different Access course related to Engineering, Mathematics, or Physics, contact us for more details.<br />\r\n- English and Mathematics GCSEs must be separate qualifications (they cannot be combined within the Access course). Typically, we require students to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 26+ points with Mathematics or Physics at a higher level.<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit.<br />\r\n- Engineering Year Zero: Pass.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you will need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each part (or equivalent).</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BEng (Hons)  Mechatronics and Robotics | De Montfort University', 'BEng (Hons)  Mechatronics and Robotics | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 05:58:40', '2024-09-21 05:58:40'),
(2815, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Media and Communication', 'ba-hons-media-and-communication', '£', '15250', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Media and Communication in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and key features of this course at DMU', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The media and communication industry greatly impacts our world, and this degree helps you become part of that change.<br />\r\nBy learning both the theory and practice of media and communications, this course will give you the skills you need to succeed in the media field.<br />\r\nThis can lead to careers in areas like PR, journalism, marketing, entertainment, international relations, politics, and education.<br />\r\nThe course is up-to-date with industry changes and uses the latest technology to keep you current.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- Career Focus: Modules cover media industries, digital cultures, and new media to help you prepare for the job market.<br />\r\n- Specialized Routes: Choose from Creative Writing, Drama, English Literature, Film Studies, History, or Journalism to complement your main studies and open more career options.<br />\r\n- Modern Facilities: Access top-notch facilities, including editing suites, TV and radio studios, dark rooms, green and blue screen studios, and video production labs.<br />\r\n- Industry Links: Benefit from connections with local media partners like BBC Radio Leicester, Phoenix Cinema and Art Centre, and community media groups.<br />\r\n- International Experience: With the DMU Global program, gain valuable international experience. Previous students have explored Hollywood, learned about Berlin&rsquo;s media history, and visited</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To apply, you need:<br />\r\n- Normally 104 UCAS points from at least two A-levels, or a BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with DMM.<br />\r\n- Five GCSEs at grade 4 or above, including English (or equivalent).</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Other accepted qualifications:<br />\r\n- Pass in a QAA-accredited Access to HE course, with a separate GCSE in English required. We usually expect students to have had a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate: 24+ points.<br />\r\n- T Levels: Merit.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each part (or equivalent) when you start the course. English language support is available through our British Council-accredited Centre for English Language Learning.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Media and Communication | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Media and Communication | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 06:03:57', '2024-09-21 06:03:57'),
(2816, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BA (Hons) Media and Communication with Modern Languages', 'ba-hons-media-and-communication-with-modern-languages', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BA (Hons) Media and Communication with Modern Languages in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and key features', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this course, you&#39;ll deeply explore how media and communications affect our lives and their role in society. Learning multiple languages can boost your job prospects, so combining this course with a language like Mandarin can make you stand out to employers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou&rsquo;ll study various subjects such as photography, video, television, and music industry management. You&rsquo;ll also investigate media representation, audience interactions, and fandoms. You can choose modules on journalism, political communication, advertising, and screenwriting to gain skills that are valuable to global employers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- Language Skills: Improve your employability by learning Mandarin, the world&rsquo;s most widely spoken language. You can start learning Mandarin at a beginner, intermediate, or advanced level.<br />\r\n- Work Placement: Gain industry experience with a work placement. Previous students have worked with BBC Radio Leicester and Phoenix Cinema.<br />\r\n- Industry Links: Benefit from connections with local media partners like BBC Radio Leicester and Phoenix Cinema.<br />\r\n- Creative Facilities: Use our advanced studios, including radio production, audio recording, and film studios with multi-camera setups and green screen facilities.<br />\r\n- Student Groups: Get hands-on experience with student groups like Demon Media, which includes The Demon magazine, Demon FM radio, Demon TV, and The Demon website. You can also join the Media and Communication Society, Film Society, and reading groups.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To apply, you need:<br />\r\n- Five GCSEs at grade C or above, including English (or equivalent).</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Plus one of the following:<br />\r\n- Normally 104 UCAS points from at least two A-levels or equivalent.<br />\r\n- BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with DMM.<br />\r\n- Pass in a QAA-accredited Access to HE course. You must have a separate GCSE in English, as it cannot be included in the Access course. We usually expect students to have had a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate with 24+ points.<br />\r\n- T Levels with a Merit grade.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each part (or equivalent).</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BA (Hons) Media and Communication with Modern Languages | De Montfort University', 'BA (Hons) Media and Communication with Modern Languages | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 06:07:09', '2024-09-21 06:07:09'),
(2817, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BSc (Hons) Media Production', 'bsc-hons-media-production', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BSc (Hons) Media Production in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and key features', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In today&#39;s world, digital and technical skills are essential in many industries, including TV and radio production, advertising, journalism, and PR.<br />\r\nDMU&rsquo;s Media Production course is designed to give you the technical skills and hands-on experience you need to succeed in this fast-changing field. You&rsquo;ll learn practical skills and understand the technical basics that are important for your career.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- Top Facilities: Use our specialized equipment, including audio recording studios, broadcast-standard radio studios, multi-camera TV studios, and green screen technology. Everything you need to create great content is right here.<br />\r\n- Work Placement: Gain valuable experience with a work placement. Our students have worked on live projects for Channel 4 and with top industry leaders and local businesses, often with paid opportunities.<br />\r\n- Student Societies: Join our award-winning Demon Media group to work on the radio station, TV channel, and website. You&rsquo;ll learn from industry experts, build your portfolio, and connect with other students.<br />\r\n- DMU Global: Take part in international experiences like exploring media history in Berlin, producing a documentary in Bali, or visiting NBC Studios in New York. These opportunities will help you learn about different cultures, expand your knowledge, and create memorable experiences.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To apply, you need:<br />\r\n- Normally 104 UCAS points from at least two A-levels, or a BTEC National Diploma/Extended Diploma with DMM.<br />\r\n- Five GCSEs at grade 4 or above, including English (or equivalent).</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Other accepted qualifications:<br />\r\n- Pass in a QAA-accredited Access to HE course. You must have a separate GCSE in English because it can&#39;t be included in the Access course. We usually expect students to have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.<br />\r\n- International Baccalaureate with 24+ points.<br />\r\n- T Levels with a Merit grade.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.0 overall, with at least 5.5 in each part (or equivalent).</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BSc (Hons) Media Production | De Montfort University', 'BSc (Hons) Media Production | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 06:09:54', '2024-09-21 06:09:54'),
(2818, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BMedSci (Hons) Medical Science', 'bmedsci-hons-medical-science', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BMedSci (Hons) Medical Science in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and key features', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU&rsquo;s Medical Science program focuses on putting students&rsquo; interests and learning experiences first, using Universal Design for Learning (UDL) principles and inclusive teaching methods. DMU&rsquo;s experienced staff provide excellent support and teach based on the latest scientific and clinical research.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nIn the first year, students gain basic knowledge and practical skills in chemistry, biochemistry, anatomy, physiology, microbiology, and professional skills. In the second year, they build on this knowledge by studying disease and healthcare techniques, and they learn about management principles relevant to many careers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nIn the third year, students carry out an independent research project, which can be in the lab, based on literature, or clinical. They write a scientific article and present their work as a public poster. This requires good time management, organization, research skills, strong writing, critical evaluation of scientific articles, and problem-solving abilities.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- Education 2030: A simplified &lsquo;block learning&rsquo; timetable lets you study one subject at a time, get quicker feedback, and have a better study-life balance.<br />\r\n- Accreditation: The curriculum is quality-assured by the Royal Society of Biology.<br />\r\n- Experienced Staff: The DMU team provides excellent support and teaches using current research.<br />\r\n- Inclusive Teaching: We use UDL principles to ensure all students are supported.<br />\r\n- Diverse Learning Activities: The program includes lectures, interactive seminars, workshops, lab work, and clinical skills sessions.<br />\r\n- Focused Learning: Enjoy excellent teaching time, academic support, and pastoral care.<br />\r\n- Lifelong Learning: The program supports continuous learning and helps you become an independent learner.<br />\r\n- Global Perspective: We use a variety of national and international resources to explore global issues.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">GCSEs:<br />\r\n- Five GCSEs at grade C/4 or above, including English and Maths.<br />\r\nA Levels:<br />\r\n- At least 120 points from 2 or more A Levels, including one A Level in Biology, Chemistry, or Human Biology at grade C/4 or above.<br />\r\nT Levels:<br />\r\n- Merit in Science (with an optional module in Laboratory Science).<br />\r\nBTEC:<br />\r\n- BTEC National Diploma in Science with grades Distinction/Distinction/Merit, or<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma in Science with grades Distinction/Distinction/Merit.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Access Course:<br />\r\n- 122 UCAS Tariff points from an Access to HE Diploma in Science, with Distinctions in science modules (not generic ones).<br />\r\n- English and Maths GCSEs required at grade 4 (C) or above as separate qualifications.<br />\r\n-Usually, you should have taken a break from full-time education before starting the Access course.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;International Baccalaureate:<br />\r\n- A score of 28 or more with six higher level points in Chemistry or Biology.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.5 overall. English language tuition is available through our British Council-accredited Centre for English Language Learning, both before and during the course if needed.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BMedSci (Hons) Medical Science | De Montfort University', 'BMedSci (Hons) Medical Science | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 06:20:32', '2024-09-21 06:20:32'),
(2819, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BSc (Hons) Pharmaceutical Science', 'bsc-hons-pharmaceutical-science', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BSc (Hons) Pharmaceutical Science in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and key features', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Developed by a team of pharmacy experts, this degree covers both the chemistry and engineering aspects of designing and making pharmaceutical products.<br />\r\nDMU&rsquo;s research-focused teachers have experience in pharmacy, engineering, chemistry, pharmacology, and microbiology. They work closely with pharmaceutical companies, so the curriculum is always updated to provide the advanced skills employers are looking for.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- Expertise: We have over 100 years of teaching experience in the Leicester School of Pharmacy, known for our academic and research excellence.<br />\r\n- Facilities: DMU&rsquo;s investment in specialized labs and industry-standard equipment helps you develop practical and professional skills.<br />\r\n- Employment: DMU graduates work with well-known international companies.<br />\r\n- International Focus: The program is designed with the global market in mind.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This is a final-year top-up degree for international students only. To join the program, the admissions tutor or program leader will review your previous studies to ensure they match our first and second-year content. Usually, you need an average mark of 70% with no module below 60% and a grade point average of 2.5. No interview is required.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DMU also accept mature students with non-standard qualifications and recognize other equivalent or international qualifications.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.5 or an equivalent level before starting the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BSc (Hons) Pharmaceutical Science | De Montfort University', 'BSc (Hons) Pharmaceutical Science | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 06:22:59', '2024-09-21 06:22:59'),
(2820, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'MPharm (Hons) Pharmacy', 'mpharm-hons-pharmacy', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study MPharm (Hons) Pharmacy in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and key features', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Pharmacists are experts in medicine who ensure that medicines are safely and effectively provided to patients and the public. They advise on how to take prescribed drugs, monitor for any side effects, and use their diagnostic skills to offer high-quality, patient-centred care.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nWith over 100 years of experience, the Leicester School of Pharmacy will help you gain the practical and professional skills needed to become a pharmacist. As pharmacy is the third largest healthcare profession in the UK, there are many diverse career opportunities available.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- Practical Placements: Gain hands-on experience with integrated placements in community, GP, and hospital settings throughout all four years of the course. You&#39;ll develop core consultation and prescribing skills under supervision.<br />\r\n- Modern Facilities: DMU&#39;s new facilities include clinical simulation suites, a hospital ward, and counselling rooms, providing you with the space to build your professional and patient care skills.<br />\r\n- Teamwork Training: DMU&rsquo;s Interprofessional Education (IPE) approach helps you learn how to work effectively with other healthcare professionals, a crucial skill for improving patient care.<br />\r\n- Research Opportunities: Work alongside experts on real-world research projects, such as those supporting healthcare professionals during the COVID-19 pandemic, and see how our award-winning projects improve patient care.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">GCSEs:<br />\r\n- Five GCSEs at grade C/4 or above, including English and Maths.<br />\r\nA-Level:<br />\r\n- At least 120 points from 3 A-Levels, including Chemistry and at least one of these at grade B or above: Biology, Maths, Physics, or Psychology. (General Studies is not accepted.)<br />\r\nBTEC:<br />\r\n- BTEC National Diploma in Science with grades Distinction/Distinction/Merit, plus Chemistry A-Level at grade B.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nAlternative Qualifications:</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Access to HE Diploma:<br />\r\n- Pass the Access to Science HE diploma with 120 UCAS tariff points. You need 15 credits at distinction in Chemistry and 15 credits at merit in other science subjects (Biology, Maths, Physics, Psychology).<br />\r\n- English and Maths GCSEs at grade C/4 are required separately. Equivalents are not accepted.<br />\r\nInternational Baccalaureate:<br />\r\n- A score of 30+ points with six higher level points in Chemistry and another science subject (Biology, Physics, Psychology, or Maths).</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.5 overall, with no less than 6.0 in each section (or an equivalent score) when you start the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'MPharm (Hons) Pharmacy | De Montfort University', 'MPharm (Hons) Pharmacy | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 06:27:01', '2024-09-21 06:27:01');
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `country_id`, `university_id`, `campus_id`, `level_id`, `budget_id`, `name`, `slug`, `currency`, `fees`, `scholarship`, `description`, `overview`, `entry_requirements`, `scholarship_details`, `url`, `title`, `share_title`, `keywords`, `page_image`, `status`, `created_by`, `updated_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(2821, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'BSc (Hons)  Psychology', 'bsc-hons-psychology', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study BSc (Hons)  Psychology in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and key features', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Psychology is the scientific study of the mind and how it affects our behavior. In this course, you&rsquo;ll explore human behavior using scientific methods like observation, measurement, and testing to understand why people act the way they do.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You&rsquo;ll cover key areas such as biological, cognitive, developmental, and social psychology. You&rsquo;ll also study personality, intelligence, research methods, and the history of psychology. There&rsquo;s an option to do a work experience placement to see how theory is used in real life. Our facilities include computer labs with the latest software, research cubicles, interview rooms, and an observation suite, all supported by our psychology technicians.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A psychology degree will help you develop valuable skills that employers want, such as critical thinking, data analysis, communication (written, oral, and visual), numerical reasoning, computer skills, teamwork, project management, and meeting deadlines. These skills make psychology graduates appealing to employers and competitive in the job market.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">An accredited psychology degree is a crucial step for becoming a psychologist or moving on to further study. It opens doors to specialized training in areas like clinical psychology, health psychology, educational psychology, and forensic psychology.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">GCSEs:</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Five GCSEs at grade 4 or above, including English and Maths.<br />\r\n- A-Levels:</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">At least 112 points from at least two A-Levels.<br />\r\nT Levels:</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Merit.<br />\r\nBTEC:</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- BTEC National Diploma: Distinction/Merit/Merit.<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma: Distinction/Merit/Merit.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Alternative Qualifications:</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Access to HE Diploma:</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- Pass with 112 UCAS tariff points, including at least 30 Level 3 credits at Merit.<br />\r\n- English GCSE is required separately. No equivalencies within the Access qualification.<br />\r\n- DMu usually prefers students to have had a break from full-time education before taking the Access course.<br />\r\nInternational Baccalaureate:</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">- 30+ points.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>English Language Requirements</strong><br />\r\nIf English isn&rsquo;t your first language, you need an IELTS score of 6.5 overall.<br />\r\nEnglish Language Support. English language help is available from our British Council-accredited Centre for English Language Learning, both before and during the course if needed.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'BSc (Hons)  Psychology | De Montfort University', 'BSc (Hons)  Psychology | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 06:30:20', '2024-09-21 06:30:20'),
(2822, 2, 12, 6, 6, 7, 'Social Work BA (Hons)', 'social-work-ba-hons', '£', '16250', '2000', 'Want to study Social Work BA (Hons) in the UK? Check the scholarship entry requirements and key features', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Would you like to make a positive impact on society? Social workers are crucial in helping and supporting people. DMU degree prepares you to be a skilled, confident, and effective social worker. The course covers everything you need to know about social work, including theories, methods, laws, and practical skills.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\nYou will learn from experienced staff how to work with both adults and children and will be ready to work in any area of social work after graduation.<br />\r\nSocial workers help in many areas, including child protection, support for vulnerable adults, elderly care, and mental health.<br />\r\nAfter finishing this degree, you can apply to become a registered social worker with Social Work England.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>Key Features:</strong><br />\r\n- DMU staff have a lot of experience in social work and teaching, making sure your learning is current and relevant.<br />\r\n- People with real-life experience are involved in teaching and assessments, providing valuable insights.<br />\r\n- The course prepares you to work with both adults and children, so you can enter various social work fields after graduation.<br />\r\n- You&#39;ll complete two practical placements in different settings (like government, voluntary, and charity services) working with children, young people, and adults. These placements will enhance your learning and job prospects.<br />\r\n- You&#39;ll develop skills by working with students and professionals from other fields, such as nurses, doctors, police, and teachers.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">GCSEs<br />\r\n- Five GCSEs at grade C/4 or above, including English and/or English Literature.<br />\r\n- We will also accept Key Skills or Functional Skills in Adult Literacy at Level 2 as an alternative to GCSEs.<br />\r\nPlus one of the following:<br />\r\nA Levels:<br />\r\n- At least 120 points from two or more A Levels.<br />\r\nBTEC:<br />\r\n- BTEC National Diploma &ndash; Distinction/Distinction/Merit.<br />\r\n- BTEC Extended Diploma &ndash; Distinction/Distinction/Merit.<br />\r\nT Levels:<br />\r\n- Merit.<br />\r\n- Access to HE Diploma (started after September 2014):<br />\r\n- Pass the Access qualification with a total of 120 UCAS points.<br />\r\n- GCSE English at grade C/4 or above, or an equivalent qualification.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />\r\n<strong>English Language Requirements</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If English is not your first language, you will need an IELTS score of 7.0 or equivalent before starting the course. English language support is available from our British Council-accredited Centre for English Language Learning (CELL), both before and during the course.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students admitted to undergraduate study at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;1,500 for their first year of study. Students commencing Postgraduate Taught study (but not the Global MBA) at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship for their first year of study up to &pound;2,000. Students admitted into the Global MBA at DMU are automatically awarded an international scholarship of &pound;2,500.</p>', 'null', 'Social Work BA (Hons) | De Montfort University', 'Social Work BA (Hons) | De Montfort University', NULL, NULL, 1, 15, NULL, '2024-09-21 06:35:10', '2024-09-21 06:35:10'),
